//@version=6
// ORBIB - three setups, one script, one equity curve.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
//   Halyard is a 15-minute opening-range break that fires on the 15m CLOSE. Break-then-Pullback (ORB + IB) is a
//   pullback-limit engine that wants a fast chart. Run separately you cannot see their combined equity curve,
//   because a chart has one timeframe and Halyard would only be right on a 15m chart.
//   Here Halyard builds its own 15-minute bars out of whatever bars the chart is showing, so the WHOLE file can
//   be run on a 1-MINUTE chart and Halyard still trades exactly the 15m opens, highs, lows and closes it would
//   have traded on a 15m chart. Run this on 1m: ORB/IB get the resolution their limit fills need, Halyard is
//   unaffected by the chart timeframe, and the Strategy Tester shows the three of them together.
//
// EXITS: TARGET OR STOP ONLY - NO CLOCK  (the "Hold trades until TP or SL" switch, ON by default)
//   Every time-based exit in this file is switched OFF by that input. A filled trade is closed by its TAKE
//   PROFIT or its STOP LOSS and by nothing else, so it can run past the 15:30 ET flatten, through the Asian
//   and London sessions, and into the next day - for as many days as it takes. What is still time-based is
//   ENTRY management only: an UNFILLED limit is cancelled at 15:30 ET so nothing rests overnight, and each
//   engine's entry windows are unchanged.
//   THE ONE EXCEPTION is the daily max-loss circuit breaker, which is a risk rule, not a clock: if it is armed
//   (it ships at 0 = off) and the day's loss is hit, everything open is closed, carried trades included.
//
//   >>> YOU MUST RUN THIS CHART WITH EXTENDED TRADING HOURS ("ETH") ON. <<<
//   The stop and the target can only fill on bars the chart actually has. With a Regular-Trading-Hours chart
//   there are no Asian or London bars at all, so an overnight trade sits untouched until 09:30 ET the next
//   morning and then fills at whatever gap price the open prints. Turn ETH on (chart settings -> Symbol ->
//   Extended trading hours, or the "ETH" session on a continuous futures contract) and the overnight bars are
//   there for the exits to trade against.
//
//   BECAUSE A TRADE CAN NOW SPAN SESSIONS, an open trade OWNS ITS ENGINE until it closes: while an ORB trade
//   is still running the ORB engine takes no new setup, even after the next 09:30 open, and the same for IB
//   and Halyard. That is the same one-trade-at-a-time seat rule the file always had, just extended across the
//   day boundary - it can never stack two trades or reverse one into another.
//
// THE 15-MINUTE ENGINE (Halyard), in short
//   Every chart bar is put in a 15-minute bucket (UTC-aligned, which is where TradingView's own 15m bars sit).
//   The LAST chart bar of a bucket closes that 15m bar, so on a 1m chart the 09:44 bar closes the 09:30-09:45
//   candle - with process_orders_on_close = true the entry fills at that bar's close, i.e. at the 15m close
//   price itself. A bucket that ends inside a data gap is caught up on the first bar of the next bucket.
//   REQUIREMENT: use a chart timeframe that divides into 15 - 1, 3, 5 or 15 minutes. On anything larger the
//   "15m" bar degrades to the chart bar and Halyard's levels stop matching a real 15m chart.
//
// HOW THE THREE SETUPS SHARE ONE POSITION
//   Pine nets every order into ONE position: an opposite-side entry would REVERSE another setup's trade, not
//   hedge it. So the seat is taken by one setup at a time, in this order of precedence:
//     1. A live HALYARD trade holds the seat. ORB and IB limits are HELD BACK (not cancelled) while it runs; if
//        price trades through their pullback entry during the hold, that setup is forfeited for the day.
//     2. A live ORB trade holds the seat against IB (the original ORB/IB rule, unchanged).
//     3. Halyard SKIPS its break if an ORB or IB trade is live. Halyard is a market order at the 15m close -
//        it cannot rest and wait - and its break still consumes the day, exactly like any other rejected filter.
//   Each engine flattens only its OWN entries (strategy.close per entry id). With the clock exits off, neither
//   the 13:30/14:30 ET Halyard boundary nor the 15:30 ET flatten closes anything at all - they only cancel
//   unfilled entry orders.
//   ONE rule still reaches across all three: the daily max-loss circuit breaker, because that is its job. It
//   closes the POSITION (cancel_all + close_all) rather than a list of entry ids, since Pine nets positions and
//   an order from one setup can end up reducing another setup's entry. EVERY close cancels first - a resting
//   limit can still fill behind a close, and a live exit order holds the position quantity reserved.
//
// PROGRESSIVE SIZING (ORB / IB) - the default sizing mode
//   Contracts follow the account up and down in fixed $6,000 rungs, measured from the starting capital:
//
//     equity          ORB (first / add)     IB (first / add)
//     ---------------------------------------------------------
//     $30,000  base         1 / 1                2 / 2
//     $36,000  +1 rung      2 / 2                4 / 4
//     $42,000  +2 rungs     3 / 3                6 / 6
//     $48,000  +3 rungs     4 / 4                8 / 8
//
//   And back down the same ladder: give $6,000 back and the size drops a rung, so $42k -> $36k takes ORB from
//   3 to 2 and IB from 6 to 4. The rung is a FULL step in both directions - $35,999 is still the base size and
//   so is $29,999; only a complete $6,000 below the base ($24,000) steps down past it, where the two MINIMUM
//   inputs decide what happens: they ship at the base size (ORB 1, IB 2), so by default the ladder never
//   trades smaller than it started, and setting a minimum to 0 stops that engine trading instead.
//
//   The rung is read from CLOSED equity (starting capital + net profit), not from the floating value of an open
//   trade, so a trade swinging in and out of profit cannot change the size of the setup being armed beside it.
//   Size is fixed when a setup ARMS - at 09:45 for ORB, 10:30 for IB - and does not move after that.
//   Halyard is NOT on this ladder: it has its own sizing block (fixed 4 contracts as shipped).
//
// RISK/REWARD BOXES: all three setups draw the SAME box - a green reward box from the entry to the target, a
//   red risk box from the entry to the stop, a coloured border per setup (orange ORB, teal IB, fuchsia
//   Halyard) and one label carrying contracts, $ risk, $ reward, the R multiple and the 1-contract numbers.
//   The box grows bar by bar for as long as the trade is open, so a multi-day trade draws a multi-day box.
//
// WHAT CHANGED vs THE TWO STANDALONE FILES
//   - One strategy() call, so ONE set of properties: commission $0.5/contract and 1 tick slippage (the ORB/IB
//     settings) now apply to Halyard too, which shipped with zero of both. Halyard's share of the curve will
//     therefore read slightly worse here than in its own backtest. Change it in Properties if you want parity.
//   - process_orders_on_close = true (Halyard needs the 15m close as its fill). ORB/IB exits are stops and
//     limits, which fill intrabar either way; their entry limits become live at the close of the break bar
//     instead of the next bar's open, which is what the engine's own fill tracking already assumed.
//   - initial_capital 30000 - the account the progressive ladder below is written for. CHANGE IT IN
//     PROPERTIES AND THE LADDER FOLLOWS: its base rung defaults to whatever the initial capital is set to.
strategy("ORBIB", overlay = true, pyramiding = 6,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500,
     initial_capital = 30000, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, process_orders_on_close = true,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.5, slippage = 1)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mode: strategy or indicator
// Pine decides strategy() vs indicator() when the script compiles, so an input cannot change the file's type.
// What this switch does is silence every ORDER. In Indicator mode the ranges, levels, fib lines, risk/reward
// boxes, probability table and break alerts all keep running on identical rules - the chart is byte for byte
// the same - while nothing is bought or sold. All three state machines (Halyard included) run in both modes,
// so the boxes you see as an indicator are exactly the trades the strategy would have taken.
gMode     = "Mode"
runMode   = input.string("Strategy - place orders", "Run as", options = ["Strategy - place orders", "Indicator - drawings & alerts only"], group = gMode,
     tooltip = "STRATEGY: the full engine - entries, exits and the daily-loss halt. INDICATOR: none of those, so no trades and an empty Strategy Tester, but every level, box, label, table and break alert still works.")
ordersOn  = runMode == "Strategy - place orders"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Exit rules
// THE ONE SETTING THAT DECIDES WHETHER THE CLOCK CAN CLOSE A TRADE.
gExit      = "Exit rules"
holdToTPSL = input.bool(true, "Hold trades until TP or SL (no time-based exit)", group = gExit,
     tooltip = "ON (default): a filled trade is closed ONLY by its take profit or its stop loss. It runs through the 15:30 ET flatten, through the Asian and London sessions and into the next day, for as long as it takes. The 15:30 ET flatten and Halyard's 13:30/14:30 ET day flat still cancel UNFILLED entry orders, so nothing new rests overnight, and Halyard's bar-count time stop is ignored.\n\nREQUIRES AN EXTENDED-HOURS CHART. The exits can only fill on bars that exist: on a Regular-Trading-Hours chart there are no overnight bars, so the trade sits until the next 09:30 ET open and fills on the gap.\n\nAn open trade OWNS ITS ENGINE until it closes - that engine takes no new setup the next day while it runs.\n\nThe daily max-loss circuit breaker still closes everything, carried trades included: it is a risk rule, not a clock.\n\nOFF: the original behaviour - Halyard flat at 13:30/14:30 ET, ORB/IB flat at 15:30 ET, plus Halyard's bar-count time stop if it is set.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy toggles (isolate each for backtesting)
gStrat    = "Strategies (toggle to track each separately)"
runHAL    = input.bool(true, "Run HALYARD strategy (15m break, timeframe-independent)", group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest ORB/IB alone.")
runORB    = input.bool(true, "Run ORB strategy", group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the IB strategy alone in the Strategy Tester.")
runIB     = input.bool(true, "Run IB strategy",  group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the ORB strategy alone.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Trade-day filters (see which weekday hurts each)
gDayO     = "Trade days - ORB"
orbMon    = input.bool(true, "ORB Monday",    group = gDayO)
orbTue    = input.bool(true, "ORB Tuesday",   group = gDayO)
orbWed    = input.bool(true, "ORB Wednesday", group = gDayO)
orbThu    = input.bool(true, "ORB Thursday",  group = gDayO)
orbFri    = input.bool(true, "ORB Friday",    group = gDayO)
gDayI     = "Trade days - IB"
ibMon     = input.bool(true, "IB Monday",    group = gDayI)
ibTue     = input.bool(true, "IB Tuesday",   group = gDayI)
ibWed     = input.bool(true, "IB Wednesday", group = gDayI)
ibThu     = input.bool(true, "IB Thursday",  group = gDayI)
ibFri     = input.bool(true, "IB Friday",    group = gDayI)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk sizing (PER ENTRY) - ORB / IB
// TWO ways to size, one active at a time - tick the one you want; each is followed by its own inputs.
// Either way the four entries are sized independently: ORB first, ORB average-down, IB first, IB average-down,
// so the add can be bigger, smaller or the same as the entry it doubles up on.
// Halyard has its own sizing block further down - it is a different setup with a different stop.
gRisk       = "Risk sizing - ORB / IB"
mFixed      = input.bool(true,  "1) Fixed contract size", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1 (default). Trade exactly the four contract counts below - no risk maths at all. If both modes are ticked this one wins; if neither is ticked this one is used.")
orbQty1In   = input.float(1, "   ORB contracts - FIRST entry",    minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the first ORB unit (the limit at the fib pullback).")
orbQty2In   = input.float(1, "   ORB contracts - AVG-DOWN entry", minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the ORB average-down unit. Independent of the first entry - larger to scale in, smaller to add only a probe.")
ibQty1In    = input.float(2, "   IB contracts - FIRST entry",     minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the first IB unit.")
ibQty2In    = input.float(2, "   IB contracts - AVG-DOWN entry",  minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the IB average-down unit.")
mDlr        = input.bool(false, "2) Risk $ per trade", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Ignore the contract counts: size each entry so ITS OWN risk equals that entry's dollar amount below. The stop distance decides the count, so a wide range buys fewer contracts and a tight one more. Untick mode 1 for this to take effect. If the amount cannot cover a single contract at that stop distance, the setup is skipped.")
orbRiskDlr1 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk - FIRST entry",     minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Dollars risked on the first ORB entry, entry to stop.")
orbRiskDlr2 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk - AVG-DOWN entry",  minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Dollars risked on the ORB average-down unit. Its stop is the same price but its entry is deeper, so the same dollars buy more contracts than the first entry - lower it if you do not want the add to dominate the setup.")
ibRiskDlr1  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk - FIRST entry",      minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk)
ibRiskDlr2  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk - AVG-DOWN entry",   minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk)
mProg       = input.bool(true,  "3) Progressive contracts (equity ladder) - OVERRIDES modes 1 and 2", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3, and the one this file ships with. Contracts climb a ladder as the account grows and come back down as it shrinks: start at the base counts below, then add the 'per rung' counts for every full step of profit above the base equity, and subtract them for every full step below it.\n\nAs shipped on a $30,000 account with $6,000 rungs: $30k = ORB 1/1 and IB 2/2, $36k = ORB 2/2 and IB 4/4, $42k = ORB 3/3 and IB 6/6 - and the same ladder in reverse on the way down.\n\nTicked, it wins over BOTH other modes. Untick it to go back to mode 1 or 2.")
progStep    = input.float(6000, "   Equity per rung ($)", minval = 1, step = 500, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. How much the account has to gain before every unit is raised by its 'per rung' count - and how much it has to give back before they come down again. A rung is a FULL step in both directions: at $6,000 rungs off a $30,000 base, $35,999 is still base size and so is $29,999.")
progBaseIn  = input.float(0, "   Base equity ($, 0 = use initial capital)", minval = 0, step = 1000, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. The equity the base contract counts belong to - the bottom rung of the ladder. 0 (the default) reads the strategy's own initial capital, which ships at $30,000 and is editable in the Properties tab, so the ladder follows whatever account size you backtest. Set a number here only if you want the ladder anchored somewhere other than your starting capital.")
progUseOpen = input.bool(false, "   Count an open trade's profit in the rung", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. OFF (default): the rung is read from CLOSED equity - initial capital plus net profit of finished trades - so an open trade swinging around cannot change the size of the next setup. ON: floating profit counts too, which makes the size move while a trade is running.")
progOrbQ1   = input.float(1, "   ORB contracts at base - FIRST entry",    minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Contracts on the first ORB unit at base equity.")
progOrbQ2   = input.float(1, "   ORB contracts at base - AVG-DOWN entry", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Contracts on the ORB average-down unit at base equity.")
progOrbAdd  = input.float(1, "   ORB contracts added per rung (each unit)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Added to EACH ORB unit for every full rung above the base equity, and taken off again for every full rung below it.")
progOrbMin  = input.float(1, "   ORB minimum contracts (0 = stop trading)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. The floor the ORB ladder cannot go under. It ships at the base size, so the ladder steps DOWN normally while it is above base (a $42k -> $36k give-back takes ORB from 3 to 2) but never trades smaller than it started. Set 0 to let it go to zero instead, which stops the ORB engine taking trades once equity is a full rung below the base.")
progIbQ1    = input.float(2, "   IB contracts at base - FIRST entry",     minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Contracts on the first IB unit at base equity.")
progIbQ2    = input.float(2, "   IB contracts at base - AVG-DOWN entry",  minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Contracts on the IB average-down unit at base equity.")
progIbAdd   = input.float(2, "   IB contracts added per rung (each unit)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. Added to EACH IB unit for every full rung above the base equity, and taken off again for every full rung below it.")
progIbMin   = input.float(2, "   IB minimum contracts (0 = stop trading)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. The floor the IB ladder cannot go under - same rule as the ORB minimum above.")
progMaxQty  = input.float(0, "   Max contracts per unit (0 = no cap)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 3. A hard ceiling on any one unit, applied after the ladder. 0 (default) leaves the ladder uncapped, so a long winning backtest keeps compounding the size - set a number here if you want the results to stay inside a size you could actually fill.")
maxDayLoss  = input.float(0, "Daily max loss $ (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "A flat dollar stop for the whole day, counted from the equity at the 09:30 session open and including open floating P&L. The moment the day is down this much, EVERY open trade - Halyard and any trade carried over from a previous day included - is closed at market, every resting order is cancelled and no new setup is taken until the next session; the block latches. NOTE the baseline resets at 09:30 ET, so a carried trade is measured on TODAY'S movement, not on the P&L it already had. 0 turns it off. Needs the strategy engine, so it does nothing in Indicator mode.")

// ONE mode only, in this order: progressive wins if it is ticked; otherwise fixed contracts wins if both of the
// other two are ticked, and is also the fallback if neither is.
rmProg     = mProg
rmFixed    = not rmProg and (mFixed or not mDlr)
sizeByRisk = not rmProg and not rmFixed
modeTxt    = rmProg ? "Sizing: progressive ladder" : rmFixed ? "Sizing: fixed contracts" : "Sizing: risk $ per entry"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the progressive ladder (ORB / IB)
// The rung this bar sits on. TRUNCATION TOWARD ZERO is the whole point of the two branches: floor() alone would
// drop a rung the moment equity slipped one dollar under the base, while a rung UP needs a full step. Rounding
// toward zero makes both directions symmetric - a full step of profit to climb, a full step of give-back to
// drop - so +$5,999 and -$5,999 are both still the base size, and -$6,000 is the first rung down.
progBaseEq = progBaseIn > 0 ? progBaseIn : strategy.initial_capital
// CLOSED equity by default: initial capital plus the net profit of finished trades. strategy.equity would add
// the floating P&L of whatever is open, which would move the size of a setup being armed beside a live trade.
progEq     = progUseOpen ? strategy.equity : strategy.initial_capital + strategy.netprofit
// IN INDICATOR MODE THE LADDER NEVER MOVES. Nothing is bought or sold there, so net profit stays 0 and the rung
// stays at base - the boxes will always show the base contract counts. Read the sizes off the Strategy Tester.
progRaw    = progStep > 0 ? (progEq - progBaseEq) / progStep : 0.0
progLevel  = progRaw >= 0 ? math.floor(progRaw) : math.ceil(progRaw)

// base + rungs, floored at the minimum and capped if a cap is set. Returns contracts for ONE unit.
f_prog(float baseQty, float addQty, float minQty) =>
    q  = baseQty + progLevel * addQty
    qm = math.max(q, minQty)
    progMaxQty > 0 ? math.min(qm, progMaxQty) : qm

progOrb1 = f_prog(progOrbQ1, progOrbAdd, progOrbMin)
progOrb2 = f_prog(progOrbQ2, progOrbAdd, progOrbMin)
progIb1  = f_prog(progIbQ1,  progIbAdd,  progIbMin)
progIb2  = f_prog(progIbQ2,  progIbAdd,  progIbMin)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Position sizing
gHPS          = "Halyard - Position sizing"
halUseRiskSz  = input.bool(false, "Use $ Risk Position Sizing", group = gHPS, tooltip = "OFF by default: Halyard trades the fixed contract count below and the Risk Per Trade ($) figure is not read at all. Tick it to size from the dollar risk instead.")
halRiskUSD    = input.float(535, "Risk Per Trade ($)", minval = 0, group = gHPS, tooltip = "UNREAD while $ Risk Position Sizing is off.")
halQtyFixed   = input.int(4, "Contracts (If Risk Sizing Off)", minval = 1, group = gHPS, tooltip = "The live setting, since $ Risk Position Sizing ships OFF.")
halMaxQty     = input.int(1000, "Max Contracts", minval = 1, group = gHPS, tooltip = "Hard cap on the risk-sized quantity.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Trade management
// Both R:R inputs are exposed, not just the first: the reverse one is UNREAD while the toggle is off but goes
// LIVE the moment it is ticked, and shipping a toggle that silently arms a hidden number is a trap.
gHTM          = "Halyard - Trade management"
halRR         = input.float(0.9, "Risk:Reward (First Trade)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.01, group = gHTM)
halRevOn      = input.bool(true, "Enable Reverse Trade", group = gHTM, tooltip = "ON by default. Also sets the day's fill cap: 2 on, 1 off - so the Risk:Reward (Reverse Trade) input below IS read. NOTE that with the clock exits off a first trade can still be running when the day ends, and the reversal only exists after that first trade has CLOSED AT A LOSS - so a trade carried overnight simply postpones or cancels the reversal.")
halRevRR      = input.float(1.0, "Risk:Reward (Reverse Trade)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.01, group = gHTM, tooltip = "Only read while Enable Reverse Trade is on.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Day filter
// One direction setting per weekday. "Off" is a day that never trades.
gHD           = "Halyard - Day filter"
halDayTip     = "Read on the SESSION's day, which ends 13:30 / 14:30 ET - not on the calendar day."
halMon        = input.string("Long", "Monday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD, tooltip = halDayTip)
halTue        = input.string("Both", "Tuesday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halWed        = input.string("Both", "Wednesday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halThu        = input.string("Both", "Thursday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halFri        = input.string("Both", "Friday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Range filter
// A DAY gate on the range candle's own size, in POINTS. 0 = off on either side. BOTH SHIP AT 0, so this
// changes nothing until a value is set.
gHR           = "Halyard - Range filter"
halRngMin     = input.float(0, "Min ORB Range (pts, 0=off)", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = gHR, tooltip = "Skip the day if the range is narrower than this.")
halRngMax     = input.float(0, "Max ORB Range (pts, 0=off)", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = gHR, tooltip = "Skip the day if the range is wider than this.")

// Min above Max passes on NOTHING, and a strategy that silently stops trading reads as "no signals today"
// rather than as a typo. Fail loudly instead.
if halRngMax > 0 and halRngMin > halRngMax
    runtime.error("Halyard Range Filter: Min ORB Range is above Max ORB Range, so no day can ever pass. Fix one of them.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Filters (ORB / IB)
// THE CLOSE-DEPTH FILTER SHIPS OFF. Both depths default to 100, which accepts a close anywhere inside the
// range and leaves only the which-extreme-came-first test deciding direction. Lower either one to switch that
// side's filter back on - 50 is the classic rule.
gFilt     = "Filters - ORB / IB"
noDbl     = input.bool(true, "Skip double-break days (both range sides break)", group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "If the side OPPOSITE the setup direction also breaks (long: price trades below the range low; short: above the range high), cancel the pending entry and take no trade that day.")
orbDepth  = input.float(100, "ORB bias: max close depth into the range (%)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "How far the range may CLOSE into its own body and still count. Depth is measured from the level that will break: for a short that is the range low, for a long the range high. 100 (the default) DISABLES the filter - any close passes, leaving only the which-extreme-came-first test. 50 is the classic rule.")
ibDepth   = input.float(100, "IB bias: max close depth into the range (%)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "Same measurement as the ORB depth filter, applied to the 1-hour initial-balance range. 100 (the default) disables it.")
orbMinRngPct = input.float(0.40, "Min ORB range (% of price, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "Skip ORB setups whose 15-min opening range is smaller than this % of price (range / range-low * 100). IB is NOT filtered. Set 0 to disable.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (manual trading)
grpBA     = "Break alerts (manual)"
brkAlerts = input.bool(true, "Alert when a range breaks (Halyard / ORB / IB)", group = grpBA,
     tooltip = "Fires a notification the moment a range breaks, with the direction and the planned entry/stop/target so you can place the trade yourself. Create ONE alert on this strategy with condition 'alert() function calls only'.\n\nThese are the ONLY alerts this script emits, and they are plain readable text meant for a HUMAN - a phone push, an email, a Telegram message. Do not point them at a broker webhook: TradingView sends anything that is not valid JSON as text/plain, and an order endpoint answers that with 415 'unsupported media type'.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk/Reward tool
grpRR     = "Risk / Reward tool"
showRR    = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward box at the break", group = grpRR)
showRR2   = input.bool(true, "  ... and a second box for the average-down unit (ORB / IB)", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The average-down unit is a trade of its own - its own entry price, contract count, risk and reward. With this on it gets its own pair of boxes (dashed border, lighter fill) measured from the 50% line to the same stop and target. It only exists on a SHALLOW setup - a deeper one enters ON the 50% line, so there is no second unit to draw.")
showRRHal = input.bool(true, "  ... and a box for the Halyard trade", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "Halyard's risk/reward box, drawn exactly like the ORB and IB ones: green reward box, red risk box, one label with contracts, $ risk, $ reward and the R multiple. Border is fuchsia so it is told apart from ORB orange and IB teal.")
showRRText = input.bool(true, "Write the numbers on the box (entry line)", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The contracts, R multiple and $ risk are printed as one small line INSIDE the reward box, pinned to the entry - the 0 line. Untick for bare boxes with no text at all. This replaces the old floating label, which needed four lines of text and covered the price action it was describing.")
showFibs  = input.bool(true, "Show fib retracement lines (25/50/75) - ORB / IB", group = grpRR, tooltip = "Dotted lines only, no text: the 25/50/75 levels of the range. Which one is the entry is shown by the R/R box.")
showInfo  = input.bool(false, "Show strategy rules panel", group = grpRR, tooltip = "Off by default - it is a reference card, not a live readout, and it covers the top-right of the chart.")
ptVal     = input.float(2.0, "$ per point per contract", group = grpRR, tooltip = "MNQ=2, NQ=20, MES=5, ES=50. Used for the ORB/IB boxes and sizing. Halyard's own box and sizing read the symbol's point value directly.")
keepBox   = input.int(0, "Keep R/R boxes for the last N setups (0 = all)", 0, 250, group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "0 keeps every past setup's boxes and fib lines. Pine caps a script at 500 boxes and 500 lines: a setup with an average-down unit draws four boxes, so that is the most recent ~125 setups.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Historical probabilities (ORB / IB)
grpP      = "Historical probabilities"
hiLive    = input.bool(true, "Highlight the live setup in the table", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Tints the table row you are currently in: the range-size row of the setup that is running, and the pullback row for the depth price has reached so far. A > marks the row that is live right now.")
showTable = input.bool(false, "Show probability table", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Off by default - it is a research readout and it covers a corner of the chart. Tick it when you want to read the odds.")
tblPos    = input.string("Bottom right", "Table position", options = ["Top right", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Top left"], group = grpP)
bMode     = input.string("Auto (equal thirds)", "Size buckets", options = ["Auto (equal thirds)", "Manual (%)"], group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Applies to the size-segmented rows only. Range is measured as % of price so buckets stay comparable as price drifts. Auto: split each strategy's own range-% distribution into three equal-count buckets (S/M/L). Manual: use the fixed % thresholds below.")
orbB1     = input.float(0.25, "Manual ORB small/med split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP, tooltip = "Used only in Manual mode.")
orbB2     = input.float(0.40, "Manual ORB med/large split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB1      = input.float(0.50, "Manual IB small/med split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB2      = input.float(0.80, "Manual IB med/large split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
pbSplit   = input.bool(false, "Split the pullback rows by size too", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "OFF (default): one 'after 25% PB' and one 'after 50% PB' row per strategy, pooled across range sizes. ON: those rows are repeated per S/M/L bucket.")
autoMode  = bMode == "Auto (equal thirds)"

// ================================================================ HARDCODED CONFIG (edit values here)
// ---- shared session clock ----
tz      = "America/New_York"
sess    = "0930-1600"
orbSess = "0930-0945"
ibSess  = "0930-1030"
flatH   = 15
flatM   = 30
// ---- ORB settings ----
orbLong   = true
orbShort  = true
orbBreak  = "Close beyond"
orbAvg    = true
orbTpL    = "Ext 10%"
orbTpS    = "Ext 30%"
orbBE     = false
orbQty1   = orbQty1In         // contracts on the first ORB entry     (Risk sizing group)
orbQty2   = orbQty2In         // contracts on the ORB avg-down entry  (Risk sizing group)
orbCutH   = 15
orbCutM   = 0
// ---- IB settings ----
ibLong    = true
ibShort   = true
ibBreak   = "Wick (touch)"
ibAvg     = true
ibTpL     = "Ext 30%"
ibTpS     = "Ext 30%"
ibBE      = false
ibQty1    = ibQty1In          // contracts on the first IB entry      (Risk sizing group)
ibQty2    = ibQty2In          // contracts on the IB avg-down entry   (Risk sizing group)
ibCutH    = 14
ibCutM    = 0
// ---- HALYARD settings ----
// Values marked UNREAD belong to a mode that is not selected - they are kept so the mode ternaries still
// compile, and a constant condition folds anyway.
// NOTE WHICH VALUES ARE LIVE: halTpType is Risk:Reward, so the Risk:Reward inputs above ARE read and
// halTpTicks / halAtrTpMult are not.
halDirection  = "Both"        // blanket override on top of the per-day grid
halSlType     = "ORB Edge + Buffer"
halSlBuf      = 0.0           // ZERO -> the stop sits exactly ON the opposite range edge
halSlTicks    = 340           // UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer
halAtrSlMult  = 3.8           // UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer
// UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer. Set halSlType = "Breakout Candle" to arm the fourth mode: the stop goes
// beyond the breakout candle instead of the far range edge, and halSlBuf is then measured past THAT extreme.
// 1 = the breakout candle alone; 2 or 3 also take in the 1-2 FIFTEEN-MINUTE candles before it (the window is
// built from the engine's own 15m bars, so it does not change with the chart timeframe), and since the level
// is the lowest low / highest high of that window, raising it can only widen the stop, never tighten it.
halSlBars     = 1
halTpType     = "Risk:Reward"
halTpTicks    = 90            // UNREAD under Risk:Reward
halAtrTpMult  = 5.0           // UNREAD under Risk:Reward
halAtrLen     = 32            // UNREAD: no ATR mode is picked
// 0 = TIME STOP OFF, and it is IGNORED ENTIRELY while "Hold trades until TP or SL" is ticked, whatever value
// is put here. Counted in 15m bars.
halMaxBars    = 0
// OFF, so there are no entry filters at all: the break, the weekday grid and the direction are the whole entry
// condition. Set true to arm the trend filter (shorts only).
halUseTrend   = false
halTrendEma   = 190
// Visual defaults. The breakout TRIANGLE marks the 15m bar that BREAKS the range, not the range candle itself.
halShowMarker = true
halUpCol      = color.new(color.green, 30)
halDnCol      = color.new(color.red, 30)
halSigCol     = color.new(color.fuchsia, 0)   // the Halyard R/R box border, vs ORB orange and IB teal

// The day's fill cap is DERIVED from the reversal switch (2 on, 1 off) rather than being a second,
// disagreeable input.
halMaxTrades = halRevOn ? 2 : 1

// ================================================================ Shared tracking (RTH session, ORB/IB clock)
inSess     = not na(time(timeframe.period, sess, tz))
newSession = inSess and not inSess[1]
var float dHigh = na
var float dLow  = na
if newSession
    dHigh := high
    dLow  := low
else if inSess
    dHigh := math.max(dHigh, high)
    dLow  := math.min(dLow, low)
tod     = hour(time, tz) * 60 + minute(time, tz)
// `flatten` is the 15:30 ET mark. With the clock exits off it no longer CLOSES anything - it only pulls
// unfilled ORB/IB entry limits so nothing new rests overnight, and it files the day's probability records.
flatten = tod >= (flatH*60 + flatM)

// ---- daily loss limit: a flat $ stop for the whole session, floating P&L included ----
// This is the ONE rule that still closes an open trade on something other than its own TP or SL, because it is
// a risk rule rather than a clock. The baseline resets at 09:30, so a trade carried in from a previous day is
// judged on what it does TODAY.
var float dayStartEq = na
var bool  dayHalt    = false
if newSession
    dayStartEq := strategy.equity
    dayHalt    := false
dayPnL = strategy.equity - dayStartEq                 // today's P&L, realised + open
if maxDayLoss > 0 and dayPnL <= -maxDayLoss
    dayHalt := true                                   // latched: the day stays shut once it trips

// day-of-week gates (per strategy) - ORB/IB read the calendar day, Halyard its own shifted session day
dow      = dayofweek(time, tz)
orbDayOK = (dow == dayofweek.monday and orbMon) or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and orbTue) or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and orbWed) or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and orbThu) or (dow == dayofweek.friday and orbFri)
ibDayOK  = (dow == dayofweek.monday and ibMon)  or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and ibTue)  or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and ibWed)  or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and ibThu)  or (dow == dayofweek.friday and ibFri)

or_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, orbSess, tz))
or_rDone = not or_inR and or_inR[1]
ib_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, ibSess, tz))
ib_rDone = not ib_inR and ib_inR[1]
var bool ibFormed = false
if newSession
    ibFormed := false
if ib_rDone
    ibFormed := true

// position sizer for ORB/IB: contracts for a $ budget at a given stop distance (points).
// round: fractional <= .5 -> down, > .5 -> up. A budget too small for a single contract returns 0, and the
// ">= 1" guards on the entries below simply skip that setup.
f_size(float budget, float ptDist) =>
    perC = ptDist * ptVal
    raw  = perC > 0 ? budget / perC : 0.0
    fr   = raw - math.floor(raw)
    fr > 0.5 ? math.ceil(raw) : math.floor(raw)

// TP resolver (ORB/IB)
f_tp(int d, float rH, float rL, float rg, float dHi, float dLo, string tpL, string tpS) =>
    d == 1 ? (tpL == "HOD/LOD" ? dHi : tpL == "Ext 10%" ? rH + 0.10*rg : tpL == "Ext 30%" ? rH + 0.30*rg : tpL == "Ext 50%" ? rH + 0.50*rg : rH) : (tpS == "HOD/LOD" ? dLo : tpS == "Ext 10%" ? rL - 0.10*rg : tpS == "Ext 30%" ? rL - 0.30*rg : tpS == "Ext 50%" ? rL - 0.50*rg : rL)

// The seat: an ORB or IB position that is open right now. Declared HERE, filled in at the bottom of the ORB/IB
// engines, and read by Halyard above them - so Halyard sees the value as of the previous chart bar. On a 1m
// chart that is a one-minute lag on a gate that only matters when a fill and a 15m close land on the same bar.
var bool orbibLive = false

// ================================================================ HALYARD ENGINE
// Single-candle opening-range breakout with an optional loser-reversal, on 15-MINUTE candles that this engine
// builds itself - so the chart can be 1m, 3m, 5m or 15m and the levels, the break and the fills are identical.
//
// The range is one 15-minute candle. The first 15m bar that CLOSES beyond it takes the day's trade and consumes
// the day whichever side it fired on - there is no second attempt if the filters reject it. Stop sits on the
// opposite edge of the range, target is a multiple of that distance.
//
// EXIT: with "Hold trades until TP or SL" ticked the trade is closed by the target or the stop and by nothing
// else - it runs past the 13:30 / 14:30 ET session roll and keeps running through Asia and London until one of
// the two levels trades. The next day's range candle still forms and the next day's break still latches, but no
// new Halyard entry can be taken while the carried trade is open (see halSeatFree / halTrDir below).
//
// The clock is HARDCODED to New York and the chart's own timezone setting moves nothing: every clock read
// passes `tz` explicitly. THE CONVERSION IS NOT A FIXED HOUR, which is the whole subtlety. The range candle is
// anchored to 10:30 Asia/Kolkata = 05:00 UTC every day of the year, because India has no DST and the US does.
// On the New York clock that is 00:00 under EST and 01:00 under EDT, so the ET hour has to FOLLOW the US
// changeover or it sits on the wrong bars for half the year. Both seasonal values are derived per bar.

// ET's UTC offset in minutes on bar `t`: 300 under EST, 240 under EDT. Read off the tape rather than assumed,
// because the entire point is that it moves. The `+ 1440 % 1440` is there because New York and UTC are usually
// on different calendar days, which sends the raw difference negative.
f_halEtOffset(t) =>
    etM = hour(t, tz) * 60 + minute(t, tz)
    (hour(t, "Etc/UTC") * 60 + minute(t, "Etc/UTC") - etM + 1440) % 1440

// 10:30 Asia/Kolkata written on the New York clock: 00:00 EST / 01:00 EDT.
f_halOrbStartMin(t) => f_halEtOffset(t) == 240 ? 60 : 0

// 00:00 Asia/Kolkata - the boundary the Halyard trading day rolls on - written on the same clock: 13:30 EST /
// 14:30 EDT. It resets the day's state and picks the day-of-week (and, with the clock exits on, force-flattens).
f_halSessionEndMin(t) => f_halEtOffset(t) == 240 ? 870 : 810

// The instant this bar's session ENDS, on the New York clock. Shifting a bar forward to its own boundary makes
// the session's date and weekday simply the ET date and weekday of the shifted instant - no wrap-around
// arithmetic anywhere, and the key and the day filter cannot drift apart because they read the same shift.
// Bumping a YYYYMMDD key by 1 instead LOOKS equivalent and is not: 20260531 + 1 is not 20260601, so every month
// boundary would split one session into two, resetting the day's state and force-flattening mid-session.
f_halSessionShift(t) => t + (1440 - f_halSessionEndMin(t)) * 60000

f_halSessionKey(t) =>
    s = f_halSessionShift(t)
    year(s, tz) * 10000 + month(s, tz) * 100 + dayofmonth(s, tz)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the 15-minute bar builder
// Buckets are aligned to the epoch, i.e. to :00/:15/:30/:45 UTC, which is exactly where TradingView's own 15m
// bars sit for these instruments (the CME reopen at 18:00 ET is on a 15-minute boundary in UTC too).
halTfMs  = 15 * 60 * 1000
chartMs  = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) * 1000
halBkt   = math.floor(time / halTfMs)

var int   halAggBkt  = na
var float halAggH    = na
var float halAggL    = na
var float halAggC    = na
var int   halAggT    = na
var bool  halBktDone = false

// set on the chart bar that CLOSES a 15-minute candle, together with that candle's H/L/C and open time
halNewBar = false
float hal15H = na
float hal15L = na
float hal15C = na
int   hal15T = na

// (1) CATCH-UP. A bucket whose last bar never arrived (a data gap, a halt, a session end) is closed here, on
//     the first bar of the next bucket, out of the aggregate as it stood. The aggregate still holds the
//     previous bar's values because it is rolled in step 2, below this.
if not na(halAggBkt) and halBkt != halAggBkt and not halBktDone
    halNewBar := true
    hal15H := halAggH
    hal15L := halAggL
    hal15C := halAggC
    hal15T := halAggT
// (2) ROLL the aggregate: start a new one on a new bucket, otherwise extend it.
if na(halAggBkt) or halBkt != halAggBkt
    halAggBkt  := halBkt
    halAggH    := high
    halAggL    := low
    halAggT    := time
    halBktDone := false
else
    halAggH := math.max(halAggH, high)
    halAggL := math.min(halAggL, low)
halAggC := close
// (3) PROJECTED CLOSE - the normal path. This chart bar is the last one of its bucket when the NEXT bar's time
//     falls in a different bucket, so the 15m candle closes here, at this bar's close. barstate.isconfirmed
//     keeps a forming bar from firing the break early.
if not halBktDone and barstate.isconfirmed and math.floor((time + chartMs) / halTfMs) != halBkt
    halBktDone := true
    halNewBar  := true
    hal15H := halAggH
    hal15L := halAggL
    hal15C := halAggC
    hal15T := halAggT

// the previous two CLOSED 15m candles, kept for the (unread) Breakout Candle stop mode; shifted at the very
// end of this engine so that during the entry logic they are still the bars BEFORE the breakout candle.
var float hal15L1 = na
var float hal15L2 = na
var float hal15H1 = na
var float hal15H2 = na

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- daily state
// Reset once per session, on the 13:30 / 14:30 ET boundary - NOT on ET midnight. NOTE what is NOT reset here:
// the live trade (halTrDir / halEnt / halStp / halTgt / halQty). A trade that is still open simply carries into
// the new session with its own stop and target intact.
halSessKey = f_halSessionKey(time)
halNewDay  = nz(ta.change(halSessKey), 0) != 0

var float halRH   = na       // the range candle's high / low / open time
var float halRL   = na
var int   halRT   = na
var bool  halBroke = false   // the day's first break latches here and consumes the day whichever side it fired on
// State machine (per day):
// 0 = no trade yet (wait for first breakout) | 1 = first trade running | 2 = first trade stopped out (wait for
// an opposite-side 15m close beyond the range) | 3 = done for the day (first trade hit TP, or reversal taken)
var int   halState  = 0
var int   halFirstDir = 0
var int   halTrades = 0
// the live (simulated AND ordered) trade
var int   halTrDir  = 0      // 0 flat, 1 long, -1 short
var float halEnt    = na
var float halStp    = na
var float halTgt    = na
var float halQty    = na
var int   halEntBar = na
var int   halBars15 = 0      // 15m candles elapsed since the entry, for the (off by default) time stop

if halNewDay
    halRH := na
    halRL := na
    halRT := na
    halBroke := false
    halState := 0
    halFirstDir := 0
    halTrades := 0

// When a 15m candle closes AND it is the range candle, store its high/low as the day's levels.
halIsRangeBar = halNewBar and (hour(hal15T, tz) * 60 + minute(hal15T, tz)) == f_halOrbStartMin(hal15T)
if halIsRangeBar
    halRH := hal15H
    halRL := hal15L
    halRT := hal15T
    halBroke := false

halLevels = not na(halRH) and not na(halRL)
halRange  = halRH - halRL

// RANGE is a DAY gate: it gates the BREAKOUT LATCH, not the entry. That distinction is the whole behaviour - a
// day the range rejects is skipped ENTIRELY (no trade, no reversal, no triangle) and is NOT consumed, because
// halBroke can only latch on a day allowed to break out in the first place. Knowable at the bars it gates: the
// range is fixed when the range candle closes, which is before anything can trade that day.
halRangeOK = not na(halRange) and (halRngMin <= 0 or halRange >= halRngMin) and (halRngMax <= 0 or halRange <= halRngMax)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- indicators (only read by unselected modes)
// Taken from the 15-MINUTE series so they do not change with the chart timeframe. request.security publishes a
// value on the first chart bar of the next 15m period, and the engine acts on the LAST bar of the current one,
// so both are the value through the candle BEFORE the breakout candle. Both are off in the shipped config.
halAtrVal = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", ta.atr(halAtrLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
halEmaVal = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", ta.ema(close, halTrendEma), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- stop / target / size
// The Breakout Candle window, over the engine's own 15m candles. Only meaningful on a bar where a 15m candle
// closed; the stop helpers are only ever called on such a bar.
halWinLow  = halSlBars >= 3 ? math.min(hal15L, math.min(nz(hal15L1, hal15L), nz(hal15L2, hal15L))) : halSlBars == 2 ? math.min(hal15L, nz(hal15L1, hal15L)) : hal15L
halWinHigh = halSlBars >= 3 ? math.max(hal15H, math.max(nz(hal15H1, hal15H), nz(hal15H2, hal15H))) : halSlBars == 2 ? math.max(hal15H, nz(hal15H1, hal15H)) : hal15H
// Floored at one tick. halSlBuf ships at 0.0, and a breakout candle that closes on its own low puts the raw
// level exactly ON the entry reference the sizer divides by, so the risk per contract would be zero and the
// size would slam into the cap. The floor is what stops that.
// NOTE the unit: halSlBuf is POINTS, not ticks. On MNQ/NQ one tick is 0.25 points.
halCandleBuf = math.max(halSlBuf, syminfo.mintick)

f_halLongStop(entryPx) =>
    halSlType == "ORB Edge + Buffer" ? halRL - halSlBuf : halSlType == "Breakout Candle" ? halWinLow - halCandleBuf : halSlType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx - halSlTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx - halAtrVal * halAtrSlMult

f_halShortStop(entryPx) =>
    halSlType == "ORB Edge + Buffer" ? halRH + halSlBuf : halSlType == "Breakout Candle" ? halWinHigh + halCandleBuf : halSlType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx + halSlTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx + halAtrVal * halAtrSlMult

// rr is only reached in Risk:Reward mode - under ATR / Fixed Ticks the first trade and the reversal get the
// SAME distance.
f_halLongTP(entryPx, stopPx, rr) =>
    halTpType == "Risk:Reward" ? entryPx + (entryPx - stopPx) * rr : halTpType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx + halTpTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx + halAtrVal * halAtrTpMult

f_halShortTP(entryPx, stopPx, rr) =>
    halTpType == "Risk:Reward" ? entryPx - (stopPx - entryPx) * rr : halTpType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx - halTpTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx - halAtrVal * halAtrTpMult

// Quantity is auto-calculated from: risk$ / (abs(entry - stop) * point value of the symbol)
f_halQty(_entry, _sl) =>
    riskPerContract = math.abs(_entry - _sl) * syminfo.pointvalue
    q = halUseRiskSz ? math.max(math.floor(halRiskUSD / (riskPerContract > 0 ? riskPerContract : syminfo.mintick * syminfo.pointvalue)), 1) : halQtyFixed
    math.min(q, halMaxQty)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- day / direction grid
// The SESSION's day-of-week, not the bar's: a bar past the 13:30 / 14:30 ET boundary already belongs to
// tomorrow's session. Read off the same shifted instant as the session key, so the two agree by construction.
halDow  = dayofweek(f_halSessionShift(time), tz)
// Saturday and Sunday fall through to "Off" - nothing here has to special-case the weekend.
halMode = halDow == dayofweek.monday ? halMon : halDow == dayofweek.tuesday ? halTue : halDow == dayofweek.wednesday ? halWed : halDow == dayofweek.thursday ? halThu : halDow == dayofweek.friday ? halFri : "Off"
halDayOK = halMode != "Off"
// The per-day setting ANDs into the global direction rather than replacing it, so the global still works as a
// blanket override on top of the per-day grid.
halLongOK  = (halDirection == "Both" or halDirection == "Long")  and (halMode == "Both" or halMode == "Long")
halShortOK = (halDirection == "Both" or halDirection == "Short") and (halMode == "Both" or halMode == "Short")
// The per-BAR filter, and it is SHORTS ONLY. It ships off. Unlike the range gate, a bar filter rejecting a
// break still CONSUMES the day - the latch fires on the break, not on the entry.
halTrendOK = not halUseTrend or (not na(halEmaVal) and hal15C < halEmaVal)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- live-trade tracking (runs in BOTH modes)
// The engine keeps its own copy of the open trade instead of reading strategy.position_size, for two reasons:
// the netted position now belongs to three setups, and Indicator mode has no position at all. The simulation
// matches the orders exactly - entry at the 15m close (process_orders_on_close), exit when price trades the
// stop or the target, stop taking precedence when a single bar covers both, which is what the Strategy Tester
// assumes as well. It runs on EVERY chart bar, session or not, so an overnight fill is seen the moment the
// Asian or London bar that reaches the level prints.
if halTrDir != 0 and bar_index > halEntBar
    halStopHit = halTrDir == 1 ? low <= halStp : high >= halStp
    halTpHit   = halTrDir == 1 ? high >= halTgt : low <= halTgt
    if halStopHit or halTpHit
        if halState == 1
            halState := halStopHit ? 2 : 3
        halTrDir := 0

// TIME STOP: flat after the Nth 15m candle from the entry. IGNORED while "Hold trades until TP or SL" is on,
// and off in the shipped config anyway (halMaxBars = 0).
if halNewBar and halTrDir != 0
    halBars15 += 1
if not holdToTPSL and halMaxBars > 0 and halTrDir != 0 and halBars15 >= halMaxBars
    if ordersOn
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Lx")                  // free the quantity the exit orders hold, or the close is dropped
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Sx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RLx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RSx")
        strategy.close("HAL-L", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-S", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-RL", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-RS", comment = "time stop")
    if halState == 1
        halState := (halTrDir == 1 ? close < halEnt : close > halEnt) ? 2 : 3
    halTrDir := 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the break
// halBroke latches the day's first break, so anything after it is ignored. The break is a 15-MINUTE close
// beyond the level; the range candle itself can never be the breakout candle.
halBrkUp = runHAL and halNewBar and not halIsRangeBar and halLevels and halRangeOK and not halBroke and hal15C > halRH
halBrkDn = runHAL and halNewBar and not halIsRangeBar and halLevels and halRangeOK and not halBroke and hal15C < halRL
// The first break consumes the day whichever side it fires on, and whether or not it passes its filters, so a
// filter can only ever REMOVE a trade, never substitute a later one.
if halBrkUp or halBrkDn
    halBroke := true

// The seat: Halyard is a market order at the 15m close and cannot rest, so a live ORB/IB trade does not delay
// it - it cancels it, and the break is still consumed. Same treatment as any other rejected filter. A HALYARD
// trade carried in from a previous session blocks the same way, through the halTrDir == 0 test on the entries.
// TWO reads of the same fact, because neither is enough on its own: orbibLive is the ORB/IB engines' own fill
// tracking, which is a chart bar stale here (those engines run below this one) but is all Indicator mode has;
// strategy.position_size is exact but only exists when orders are actually being placed. Halyard's own trade
// can never be the one showing in it - halTrDir == 0 is required below before any entry is considered.
halSeatFree = not orbibLive and not dayHalt and (not ordersOn or strategy.position_size == 0)
halEntered  = false
halEntDir   = 0

// --- First trade (take the FIRST breakout, if it passes the filters) ---
halEnterL = halBrkUp and halLongOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halState == 0
if halEnterL
    sl = f_halLongStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halLongTP(hal15C, sl, halRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halFirstDir := 1
    halState  := 1
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := 1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := 1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-L", strategy.long, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-Lx", from_entry = "HAL-L", stop = sl, limit = tp)

halEnterS = halBrkDn and halShortOK and halDayOK and halTrendOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halState == 0
if halEnterS
    sl = f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halShortTP(hal15C, sl, halRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halFirstDir := -1
    halState  := 1
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := -1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := -1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-S", strategy.short, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-Sx", from_entry = "HAL-S", stop = sl, limit = tp)

// --- Reversal trade (only if the FIRST trade closed at a LOSS) ---
// ON BY DEFAULT: Enable Reverse Trade ships ticked, so the day's cap is 2 fills and the Risk:Reward (Reverse
// Trade) input IS read. Untick it to go back to one attempt per day.
// NOT filtered. The reversal is gated on the day-of-week, the direction and the losing first trade only - the
// entry filters apply to the FIRST trade. Note the per-day direction grid DOES reach it: a weekday set to one
// side can never take the reversal, since the reversal is by definition the opposite side of the loser.
// NOTE it is a SAME-SESSION idea: halState resets at the 13:30 / 14:30 ET roll, so a first trade that is still
// running at the roll (which the hold-to-TP/SL exit now allows) never produces a reversal.
halRevL = halRevOn and runHAL and halNewBar and halState == 2 and halFirstDir == -1 and halLongOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halLevels and hal15C > halRH
if halRevL
    sl = f_halLongStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halLongTP(hal15C, sl, halRevRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halState  := 3
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := 1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := 1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-RL", strategy.long, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-RLx", from_entry = "HAL-RL", stop = sl, limit = tp)

halRevS = halRevOn and runHAL and halNewBar and halState == 2 and halFirstDir == 1 and halShortOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halLevels and hal15C < halRL
if halRevS
    sl = f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halShortTP(hal15C, sl, halRevRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halState  := 3
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := -1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := -1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-RS", strategy.short, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-RSx", from_entry = "HAL-RS", stop = sl, limit = tp)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard session roll
// WITH "Hold trades until TP or SL" ON (the default) nothing here closes a trade. The roll only cancels the
// four Halyard ENTRY ids, which is a no-op in practice - Halyard entries are market orders and never rest -
// and the trade keeps its stop and target into Asia, London and the next day.
//
// WITH THE SWITCH OFF the original behaviour is back: never carry a position past the session its levels belong
// to, i.e. past 13:30 / 14:30 ET. That must fire on the LAST bar of that session; a Pine script cannot see the
// next bar, so it projects one CHART bar forward instead - exact on every ordinary boundary. halNewDay is the
// catch-up for boundaries inside a market gap.
// KNOWN GAP in that mode: the catch-up is NOT "one bar late". On a holiday early close the tape halts at 13:00
// ET, BEFORE the boundary, so no flat fires and halNewDay does not arrive until the next session opens.
halDayFlat = not holdToTPSL and halTrDir != 0 and (f_halSessionKey(time + chartMs) != halSessKey or halNewDay)
if halDayFlat
    if ordersOn
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Lx")                  // free the quantity the exit orders hold, or the close is dropped
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Sx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RLx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RSx")
        strategy.close("HAL-L", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-S", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-RL", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-RS", comment = "day flat")
    if halState == 1
        halState := (halTrDir == 1 ? close < halEnt : close > halEnt) ? 2 : 3
    halTrDir := 0

// BELT AND BRACES for the day flat above, and it is gated on the SAME switch: with the hold on, a Halyard trade
// is MEANT to survive the roll, so a blind sweep here would undo exactly what the switch is for. What still
// happens on every roll is the entry-order cancel, so no stale Halyard entry can be sitting anywhere.
if ordersOn and halNewDay
    strategy.cancel("HAL-L")
    strategy.cancel("HAL-S")
    strategy.cancel("HAL-RL")
    strategy.cancel("HAL-RS")
    if not holdToTPSL
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Lx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-Sx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RLx")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RSx")
        strategy.close("HAL-L",  comment = "day flat (sweep)")
        strategy.close("HAL-S",  comment = "day flat (sweep)")
        strategy.close("HAL-RL", comment = "day flat (sweep)")
        strategy.close("HAL-RS", comment = "day flat (sweep)")

// live Halyard trade -> the ORB and IB limits are held back behind it (see the ORB/IB engines below)
halLive = halTrDir != 0

// shift the closed-15m-candle registers, AFTER everything above has read them as "the candles before this one"
if halNewBar
    hal15L2 := hal15L1
    hal15L1 := hal15L
    hal15H2 := hal15H1
    hal15H1 := hal15H

// ================================================================ Historical-probability stats (ORB / IB)
// TWO walk-forward studies are collected (a day is only added to the sample after its 15:30 ET mark, so the
// numbers shown on any bar never contain data from that day or later):
//
//   A) FILL -> 15:30, segmented by range size. One record per FILLED trade: did price TOUCH each level between
//      the fill and the 15:30 ET mark? Range is stored as % of price (range / range-low * 100) so the S/M/L
//      buckets stay comparable as price drifts over the years. These are the "size" rows of the table.
//
//   B) PULLBACK -> 15:30. One record per SETUP THAT BROKE its range (whether or not the order was actually
//      placed - a day where the IB was held back behind an open ORB or Halyard trade still tells you what
//      price did). It answers: once price has retraced to the 25% fib, how often does it go on to tag each TP
//      extension? And the same from the 50% fib. On the very bar that reaches the pullback, a level counts
//      only if the CLOSE is already beyond it. From the next bar on, an ordinary wick touch counts.
//      The 50% line can only be reached through the 25% line, so the 50% sample is a subset of the 25% one.
//
// BOTH STUDIES STILL STOP AT 15:30 ET, deliberately, even though a trade may now run past it: they are a
// same-day distribution of where price goes after a break, and stretching them overnight would mix a 6-hour
// window with a 20-hour one and make the percentages incomparable. Read them as "what the session did", and
// read the Strategy Tester for what the held-to-TP/SL trades actually earned.
f_pct(int hit, int n) => n > 0 ? 100.0 * hit / n : na
f_pctStr(int hit, int n) =>
    p = f_pct(hit, n)
    na(p) ? "-" : str.tostring(p, "#") + "%"

// ---- study A: one record per filled trade ----
var tRng   = array.new_float(0)
var tStrat = array.new_int(0)
var tSL100 = array.new_int(0)
var tSL75  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP0   = array.new_int(0)
var tTP10  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP30  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP50  = array.new_int(0)

f_pushTrade(int s, float rng, bool s100, bool s75, bool t0, bool t10, bool t30, bool t50) =>
    array.push(tRng,   rng)
    array.push(tStrat, s)
    array.push(tSL100, s100 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tSL75,  s75  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP0,   t0   ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP10,  t10  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP30,  t30  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP50,  t50  ? 1 : 0)

// ranges recorded so far for one strategy (walk-forward: only days finalized before now)
f_ranges(int s) =>
    tmp = array.new_float(0)
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s
                array.push(tmp, array.get(tRng, i))
    tmp

// tercile boundaries for a strategy (na until >=3 samples); in manual mode the caller passes fixed thresholds
f_b1(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 33.33333)
f_b2(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 66.66667)
f_bkt(float rng, float b1, float b2) => (na(b1) or na(b2)) ? 0 : rng < b1 ? 0 : rng < b2 ? 1 : 2

// counts [n, sl100, sl75, tp0, tp10, tp30, tp50] for one strategy+bucket given the boundaries
f_seg(int s, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nn = 0
    a0 = 0
    a1 = 0
    a2 = 0
    a3 = 0
    a4 = 0
    a5 = 0
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s and f_bkt(array.get(tRng, i), b1, b2) == bkt
                nn := nn + 1
                a0 := a0 + array.get(tSL100, i)
                a1 := a1 + array.get(tSL75,  i)
                a2 := a2 + array.get(tTP0,   i)
                a3 := a3 + array.get(tTP10,  i)
                a4 := a4 + array.get(tTP30,  i)
                a5 := a5 + array.get(tTP50,  i)
    [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5]

// ---- study B: one record per armed setup, conditioned on how deep the pullback went ----
// Level order used everywhere below: 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100.
var pbStrat = array.new_int(0)
var pbRngP  = array.new_float(0)
var pbR25   = array.new_int(0)      // did price retrace to the 25% fib
var pbR50   = array.new_int(0)      // ... and to the 50% fib
var pb25_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 25% retrace onward
var pb25_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_5  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 50% retrace onward
var pb50_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_5  = array.new_int(0)

f_pbPush(int s, float rngP, bool r25, bool r50, array<bool> h25, array<bool> h50) =>
    array.push(pbStrat, s)
    array.push(pbRngP,  rngP)
    array.push(pbR25,   r25 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pbR50,   r50 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_0, array.get(h25, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_1, array.get(h25, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_2, array.get(h25, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_3, array.get(h25, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_4, array.get(h25, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_5, array.get(h25, 5) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_0, array.get(h50, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_1, array.get(h50, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_2, array.get(h50, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_3, array.get(h50, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_4, array.get(h50, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_5, array.get(h50, 5) ? 1 : 0)

// counts for one strategy at one pullback depth. depth 0 = reached the 25% fib, 1 = reached the 50% fib.
// bkt = -1 pools all range sizes; 0/1/2 restricts to the S/M/L bucket defined by b1/b2.
// Returns [setups armed, setups that reached that pullback, then TP0, TP10, TP30, TP50, SL75, SL100 counts].
f_pbSeg(int s, int depth, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nAll = 0
    nn   = 0
    h0 = 0
    h1 = 0
    h2 = 0
    h3 = 0
    h4 = 0
    h5 = 0
    if array.size(pbStrat) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pbStrat) - 1
            if array.get(pbStrat, i) == s and (bkt < 0 or f_bkt(array.get(pbRngP, i), b1, b2) == bkt)
                nAll := nAll + 1
                if (depth == 0 ? array.get(pbR25, i) : array.get(pbR50, i)) == 1
                    nn := nn + 1
                    h0 := h0 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_0, i) : array.get(pb50_0, i))
                    h1 := h1 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_1, i) : array.get(pb50_1, i))
                    h2 := h2 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_2, i) : array.get(pb50_2, i))
                    h3 := h3 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_3, i) : array.get(pb50_3, i))
                    h4 := h4 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_4, i) : array.get(pb50_4, i))
                    h5 := h5 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_5, i) : array.get(pb50_5, i))
    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5]

// ================================================================ ORB ENGINE (runs first of the two pullbacks)
var float or_rH = na
var float or_rL = na
var int   or_rHbar = na
var int   or_rLbar = na
var int   or_dir = 0
var bool  or_shallow = false
var float or_e1 = na
var float or_e2 = na
var float or_zstop = na
var float or_rng = na
var bool  or_broke = false
var bool  or_placed = false
var bool  or_ordLive = false     // the entry limits are actually resting - cleared the moment they are cancelled
var bool  or_f1 = false
var bool  or_f2 = false
var float or_avgPx = na
var float or_curStop = na
var float or_curTP = na
var bool  or_beDone = false
var bool  or_closed = false
var bool  or_oppBroke = false
var bool  or_missed = false      // the ORB pullback traded through while a Halyard trade held the seat
var float orbSz1 = na
var float orbSz2 = na

// A TRADE THAT IS STILL OPEN AT 09:30 OWNS THE ENGINE. Skipping the daily reset is what keeps its stop, its
// target and its fill state alive across the boundary, and it also means the ORB takes no new setup that day:
// or_broke / or_placed are still true and or_closed is still false, so nothing new can be armed. When the trade
// finally hits TP or SL, or_closed latches and the engine simply sits out the rest of that day - the seat rule
// this file has always had, extended over the date change.
var bool orbCarryDay = false
orbHold = holdToTPSL and (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
// The decision is taken ONCE, at the 09:30 open, and held for the whole session. Reading it live instead would
// unfreeze the engine the moment the carried trade closed - and if that happened inside the 09:30-09:45 window
// the range builder would start extending YESTERDAY's high and low with today's bars.
if newSession
    orbCarryDay := orbHold
if newSession and not orbCarryDay
    or_rH := na
    or_rL := na
    or_dir := 0
    or_shallow := false
    or_e1 := na
    or_e2 := na
    or_zstop := na
    or_rng := na
    or_broke := false
    or_placed := false
    or_ordLive := false
    or_f1 := false
    or_f2 := false
    or_avgPx := na
    or_curStop := na
    or_curTP := na
    or_beDone := false
    or_closed := false
    or_oppBroke := false
    or_missed := false
    orbSz1 := na
    orbSz2 := na
if or_inR and not orbCarryDay
    if na(or_rH) or high > or_rH
        or_rH := high
        or_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(or_rL) or low < or_rL
        or_rL := low
        or_rLbar := bar_index
if or_rDone and not orbCarryDay and not na(or_rH) and or_rH > or_rL
    or_rng := or_rH - or_rL
    or_lf = or_rLbar < or_rHbar
    or_pos = (close[1] - or_rL) / or_rng
    orbDepF = orbDepth / 100.0                    // how deep the close may sit, measured from the breaking level
    if orbLong and or_lf and or_pos >= 1.0 - orbDepF
        or_dir := 1
        or_shallow := or_pos >= 0.75
        or_e1 := or_shallow ? or_rL + 0.75*or_rng : or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_e2 := or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_zstop := or_rL                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    else if orbShort and (not or_lf) and or_pos <= orbDepF
        or_dir := -1
        or_shallow := or_pos <= 0.25
        or_e1 := or_shallow ? or_rL + 0.25*or_rng : or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_e2 := or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_zstop := or_rH                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    if or_dir != 0
        // each unit is sized on its own budget and its own stop distance (the add sits closer to the stop)
        // SIZE IS FIXED HERE, when the setup arms at 09:45, off the rung the account is on at that moment.
        orbSz1 := rmProg ? progOrb1 : sizeByRisk ? f_size(orbRiskDlr1, math.abs(or_e1 - or_zstop)) : orbQty1
        orbSz2 := rmProg ? progOrb2 : sizeByRisk ? f_size(orbRiskDlr2, math.abs(or_e2 - or_zstop)) : orbQty2
or_useAdd = orbAvg and or_shallow and not na(or_e2)
// break by selected type
or_brk = orbBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL)) : ((or_dir == 1 and close > or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and close < or_rL))
if or_dir != 0 and or_brk and not orbCarryDay
    or_broke := true
// double-break detection: opposite range extreme is violated
if or_dir == 1 and low < or_rL and not orbCarryDay
    or_oppBroke := true
if or_dir == -1 and high > or_rH and not orbCarryDay
    or_oppBroke := true
// entry window: before IB forms (when IB is on), within ORB cutoff otherwise, on an allowed weekday
orbSizeOK = orbMinRngPct <= 0 or (not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0 and or_rng / or_rL * 100 >= orbMinRngPct)
// NO CARRY OF AN UNFILLED ORDER. The ORB window shuts the moment the IB range FORMS at 10:30: a resting ORB
// limit is cancelled there, and an ORB that breaks after 10:30 is never placed at all. The ORB owns the
// 09:45-10:30 slot and hands the day to the IB when the IB range completes. This is ENTRY management and is
// untouched by the hold-to-TP/SL exit, which only ever governs a trade that has already filled.
orbWin = inSess and not dayHalt and orbDayOK and tod <= (orbCutH*60 + orbCutM) and (not runIB or not ibFormed) and orbSizeOK
// SEAT: a live HALYARD trade holds the ORB limit back rather than cancelling it - same rule the IB has always
// had behind an open ORB. If the ORB pullback entry trades through during the hold, that fill was missed and
// the ORB is done for the day.
if runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_placed and not or_closed and halLive and not na(or_e1)
    if (or_dir == 1 and low <= or_e1) or (or_dir == -1 and high >= or_e1)
        or_missed := true
// `not halLive` is the Halyard engine's own flag, and this engine runs BELOW it only for the seat variable -
// halLive itself is current, but orbibLive (what Halyard reads) is a chart bar stale. strategy.position_size
// is the broker's own answer and cannot be stale, so it is checked too: no ORB order is placed while ANY
// position is open, whoever it belongs to - including a trade carried in from a previous session.
if runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_placed and not or_closed and orbWin and not flatten and (not noDbl or not or_oppBroke) and orbSz1 >= 1 and not halLive and not or_missed and (not ordersOn or strategy.position_size == 0)
    if ordersOn
        if or_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("ORL", strategy.long, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
            if or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("ORL2", strategy.long, qty = orbSz2, limit = or_e2)
        else
            strategy.entry("ORS", strategy.short, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
            if or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("ORS2", strategy.short, qty = orbSz2, limit = or_e2)
    or_placed  := true                      // the setup is tracked in both modes; only the order is optional
    or_ordLive := true
// FILLS ARE ONLY TRACKED WHILE THE ORDERS ARE ACTUALLY RESTING. Without the or_ordLive gate an overnight bar
// could drift back through a CANCELLED limit price and mark a fill that never happened - which used to be a
// harmless no-op and is not any more, because a "filled" trade now owns the engine into the next day.
if or_placed and or_ordLive and not or_closed
    if or_dir == 1
        if not or_f1 and low <= or_e1
            or_f1 := true
        if or_useAdd and not or_f2 and low <= or_e2
            or_f2 := true
    if or_dir == -1
        if not or_f1 and high >= or_e1
            or_f1 := true
        if or_useAdd and not or_f2 and high >= or_e2
            or_f2 := true
or_firstFill = (or_f1 or or_f2) and not (or_f1[1] or or_f2[1])
if or_f1 or or_f2
    or_avgPx := or_f1 and or_f2 ? (or_e1 + or_e2) / 2 : or_f1 ? or_e1 : or_e2
if or_firstFill
    or_curStop := or_zstop
    or_curTP := f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    or_beDone := false
if orbBE and not or_beDone and (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
    if or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH
        or_curStop := math.max(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
    if or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL
        or_curStop := math.min(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
// THE EXITS ARE RE-ISSUED EVERY BAR, and with the hold on that includes every overnight bar - which is exactly
// what keeps the stop and the target working through Asia and London. With the hold OFF they stop at the 15:30
// flatten instead: a live strategy.exit reserves the whole position quantity for itself, so a market close
// created after it would have nothing left to close and would be dropped.
if ordersOn and (holdToTPSL or not flatten) and not na(or_curStop)
    strategy.exit("ORLx",  from_entry = "ORL",  stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORL2x", from_entry = "ORL2", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORSx",  from_entry = "ORS",  stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORS2x", from_entry = "ORS2", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
// The engine's own copy of "this trade is over", checked on EVERY bar including overnight ones, so a stop or a
// target that trades at 03:00 ET is registered there and not at the next 09:30 open.
if (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed and not na(or_curStop)
    if or_dir == 1 and (low <= or_curStop or high >= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
    if or_dir == -1 and (high >= or_curStop or low <= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
// Cancel resting ORB ENTRIES once the window closes unfilled, or done/flat/off/double-break/missed. orbWin
// closes at 10:30 when the IB range forms, so that is also where an unfilled ORB limit is pulled, and `flatten`
// pulls anything still resting at 15:30 so no entry order can live overnight. Note this list is entry ids only
// - the ORLx/ORSx EXIT orders are never cancelled here, which is what lets a filled trade keep running.
orbCancel = or_closed or flatten or not runORB or or_missed or (noDbl and or_oppBroke) or ((not orbWin) and not (or_f1 or or_f2))
if ordersOn and orbCancel
    strategy.cancel("ORL")
    strategy.cancel("ORL2")
    strategy.cancel("ORS")
    strategy.cancel("ORS2")
if orbCancel
    or_ordLive := false
// ---- ORB study A: from the fill to the 15:30 mark, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  or_trk    = false
var int   or_tdir   = 0
var float orL_sl100 = na
var float orL_sl75  = na
var float orL_tp0   = na
var float orL_tp10  = na
var float orL_tp30  = na
var float orL_tp50  = na
var bool  orR_sl100 = false
var bool  orR_sl75  = false
var bool  orR_tp0   = false
var bool  orR_tp10  = false
var bool  orR_tp30  = false
var bool  orR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    or_trk := false
if or_firstFill and not na(or_rng)
    or_trk    := true
    or_tdir   := or_dir
    orL_sl100 := or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH
    orL_sl75  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng
    orL_tp0   := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL
    orL_tp10  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng
    orL_tp30  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng
    orL_tp50  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng
    orR_sl100 := false
    orR_sl75  := false
    orR_tp0   := false
    orR_tp10  := false
    orR_tp30  := false
    orR_tp50  := false
if or_trk
    if or_tdir == 1
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or high >= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or high >= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or high >= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or high >= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or low  <= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or low  <= orL_sl100
    else
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or low  <= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or low  <= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or low  <= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or low  <= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or high >= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or high >= orL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(0, or_rng / or_rL * 100, orR_sl100, orR_sl75, orR_tp0, orR_tp10, orR_tp30, orR_tp50)
        or_trk := false

// ---- ORB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the 15:30 mark ----
var bool  orP_act  = false
var int   orP_dir  = 0
var float orP_rngP = na
var float orP_p25  = na
var float orP_p50  = na
var bool  orP_r25  = false
var bool  orP_r50  = false
var orP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var orP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var orP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    orP_act := false
if or_broke and not or_broke[1] and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0
    orP_act  := true
    orP_dir  := or_dir
    orP_rngP := or_rng / or_rL * 100
    orP_p25  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * or_rng
    orP_p50  := or_rL + 0.50 * or_rng
    orP_r25  := false
    orP_r50  := false
    array.set(orP_lv, 0, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)
    array.set(orP_lv, 1, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 2, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 3, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 4, or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 5, or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(orP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(orP_h50, k, false)
if orP_act
    up    = orP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not orP_r25 and (up ? low <= orP_p25 : high >= orP_p25)
        orP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not orP_r50 and (up ? low <= orP_p50 : high >= orP_p50)
        orP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    // On the bar that REACHES the pullback the touch must be confirmed by the CLOSE: the last tick of that bar
    // is beyond the level, so it traded there after the retrace. Later bars count an ordinary wick touch.
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(orP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if orP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h25, k, true)
        if orP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(0, orP_rngP, orP_r25, orP_r50, orP_h25, orP_h50)
        orP_act := false

// ================================================================ IB ENGINE
var float ib_rH = na
var float ib_rL = na
var int   ib_rHbar = na
var int   ib_rLbar = na
var int   ib_dir = 0
var bool  ib_shallow = false
var float ib_e1 = na
var float ib_e2 = na
var float ib_zstop = na
var float ib_rng = na
var bool  ib_broke = false
var bool  ib_placed = false
var bool  ib_ordLive = false     // the entry limits are actually resting - cleared the moment they are cancelled
var bool  ib_f1 = false
var bool  ib_f2 = false
var float ib_avgPx = na
var float ib_curStop = na
var float ib_curTP = na
var bool  ib_beDone = false
var bool  ib_closed = false
var bool  ib_oppBroke = false
var bool  ib_missed = false      // the IB pullback was reached while another setup held the seat -> skip IB today
var float ibSz1 = na
var float ibSz2 = na

// Same rule as the ORB engine: an IB trade still open at 09:30 keeps its state, its stop and its target, and
// owns the IB engine for that day.
var bool ibCarryDay = false
ibHold = holdToTPSL and (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed
// Latched once at the open, exactly like the ORB engine's orbCarryDay above and for the same reason.
if newSession
    ibCarryDay := ibHold
if newSession and not ibCarryDay
    ib_rH := na
    ib_rL := na
    ib_dir := 0
    ib_shallow := false
    ib_e1 := na
    ib_e2 := na
    ib_zstop := na
    ib_rng := na
    ib_broke := false
    ib_placed := false
    ib_ordLive := false
    ib_f1 := false
    ib_f2 := false
    ib_avgPx := na
    ib_curStop := na
    ib_curTP := na
    ib_beDone := false
    ib_closed := false
    ib_oppBroke := false
    ib_missed := false
    ibSz1 := na
    ibSz2 := na
if ib_inR and not ibCarryDay
    if na(ib_rH) or high > ib_rH
        ib_rH := high
        ib_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(ib_rL) or low < ib_rL
        ib_rL := low
        ib_rLbar := bar_index
if ib_rDone and not ibCarryDay and not na(ib_rH) and ib_rH > ib_rL
    ib_rng := ib_rH - ib_rL
    ib_lf = ib_rLbar < ib_rHbar
    ib_pos = (close[1] - ib_rL) / ib_rng
    ibDepF = ibDepth / 100.0
    if ibLong and ib_lf and ib_pos >= 1.0 - ibDepF
        ib_dir := 1
        ib_shallow := ib_pos >= 0.75
        ib_e1 := ib_shallow ? ib_rL + 0.75*ib_rng : ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_e2 := ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_zstop := ib_rL                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    else if ibShort and (not ib_lf) and ib_pos <= ibDepF
        ib_dir := -1
        ib_shallow := ib_pos <= 0.25
        ib_e1 := ib_shallow ? ib_rL + 0.25*ib_rng : ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_e2 := ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_zstop := ib_rH                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    if ib_dir != 0
        // same rung, read when the IB setup arms at 10:30
        ibSz1 := rmProg ? progIb1 : sizeByRisk ? f_size(ibRiskDlr1, math.abs(ib_e1 - ib_zstop)) : ibQty1
        ibSz2 := rmProg ? progIb2 : sizeByRisk ? f_size(ibRiskDlr2, math.abs(ib_e2 - ib_zstop)) : ibQty2
// SEAT: an OPEN trade of ANY other setup keeps priority - the IB order is held back (either direction, so the
// two can never stack risk or hedge each other). The IB is not cancelled, only delayed: the moment the seat
// frees the IB limit goes in, provided price has NOT already traded through the IB entry level while it was
// held. If it has, that pullback was missed and the IB is done for the day. An ORB or Halyard trade carried in
// from a previous session holds the seat exactly the same way.
orbLive   = runORB and (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
ibHeld    = orbLive or halLive
ib_useAdd = ibAvg and ib_shallow and not na(ib_e2)
ib_brk = ibBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL)) : ((ib_dir == 1 and close > ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and close < ib_rL))
if ib_dir != 0 and ib_brk and not ibCarryDay
    ib_broke := true
if ib_dir == 1 and low < ib_rL and not ibCarryDay
    ib_oppBroke := true
if ib_dir == -1 and high > ib_rH and not ibCarryDay
    ib_oppBroke := true
ibWin = inSess and not dayHalt and ibDayOK and tod <= (ibCutH*60 + ibCutM)
// hold the IB while another trade is live; if its entry level trades through during the hold, the IB is forfeited
if runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_placed and not ib_closed and ibHeld and not na(ib_e1)
    if (ib_dir == 1 and low <= ib_e1) or (ib_dir == -1 and high >= ib_e1)
        ib_missed := true
// Same broker-truth check as the ORB placement above: never place into an already-open position.
if runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_placed and not ib_closed and ibWin and not flatten and (not noDbl or not ib_oppBroke) and ibSz1 >= 1 and not ibHeld and not ib_missed and (not ordersOn or strategy.position_size == 0)
    if ordersOn
        if ib_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("IBL", strategy.long, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
            if ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("IBL2", strategy.long, qty = ibSz2, limit = ib_e2)
        else
            strategy.entry("IBS", strategy.short, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
            if ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("IBS2", strategy.short, qty = ibSz2, limit = ib_e2)
    ib_placed  := true
    ib_ordLive := true
// fills are only tracked while the orders are actually resting - see the ORB engine for why
if ib_placed and ib_ordLive and not ib_closed
    if ib_dir == 1
        if not ib_f1 and low <= ib_e1
            ib_f1 := true
        if ib_useAdd and not ib_f2 and low <= ib_e2
            ib_f2 := true
    if ib_dir == -1
        if not ib_f1 and high >= ib_e1
            ib_f1 := true
        if ib_useAdd and not ib_f2 and high >= ib_e2
            ib_f2 := true
ib_firstFill = (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not (ib_f1[1] or ib_f2[1])
if ib_f1 or ib_f2
    ib_avgPx := ib_f1 and ib_f2 ? (ib_e1 + ib_e2) / 2 : ib_f1 ? ib_e1 : ib_e2
if ib_firstFill
    ib_curStop := ib_zstop
    ib_curTP := f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    ib_beDone := false
if ibBE and not ib_beDone and (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed
    if ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH
        ib_curStop := math.max(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL
        ib_curStop := math.min(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
// Same rule as the ORB exits above: re-issued on every bar while the hold is on, so the stop and the target are
// live overnight; with the hold off they stop at the flatten so the EOD close cannot be blocked by them.
if ordersOn and (holdToTPSL or not flatten) and not na(ib_curStop)
    strategy.exit("IBLx",  from_entry = "IBL",  stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBL2x", from_entry = "IBL2", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBSx",  from_entry = "IBS",  stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBS2x", from_entry = "IBS2", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
if (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed and not na(ib_curStop)
    if ib_dir == 1 and (low <= ib_curStop or high >= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and (high >= ib_curStop or low <= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
// entry ids only - the IBLx/IBSx exit orders are never cancelled here
ibCancel = ib_closed or flatten or not runIB or ib_missed or (noDbl and ib_oppBroke) or ((not ibWin) and not (ib_f1 or ib_f2))
if ordersOn and ibCancel
    strategy.cancel("IBL")
    strategy.cancel("IBL2")
    strategy.cancel("IBS")
    strategy.cancel("IBS2")
if ibCancel
    ib_ordLive := false

// The seat as Halyard reads it on the NEXT chart bar (declared above the Halyard engine).
orbibLive := orbLive or (runIB and (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed)
// ---- IB study A: from the fill to the 15:30 mark, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  ib_trk    = false
var int   ib_tdir   = 0
var float ibL_sl100 = na
var float ibL_sl75  = na
var float ibL_tp0   = na
var float ibL_tp10  = na
var float ibL_tp30  = na
var float ibL_tp50  = na
var bool  ibR_sl100 = false
var bool  ibR_sl75  = false
var bool  ibR_tp0   = false
var bool  ibR_tp10  = false
var bool  ibR_tp30  = false
var bool  ibR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    ib_trk := false
if ib_firstFill and not na(ib_rng)
    ib_trk    := true
    ib_tdir   := ib_dir
    ibL_sl100 := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH
    ibL_sl75  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng
    ibL_tp0   := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL
    ibL_tp10  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng
    ibL_tp30  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng
    ibL_tp50  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng
    ibR_sl100 := false
    ibR_sl75  := false
    ibR_tp0   := false
    ibR_tp10  := false
    ibR_tp30  := false
    ibR_tp50  := false
if ib_trk
    if ib_tdir == 1
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or high >= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or high >= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or high >= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or high >= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or low  <= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or low  <= ibL_sl100
    else
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or low  <= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or low  <= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or low  <= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or low  <= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or high >= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or high >= ibL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(1, ib_rng / ib_rL * 100, ibR_sl100, ibR_sl75, ibR_tp0, ibR_tp10, ibR_tp30, ibR_tp50)
        ib_trk := false

// ---- IB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the 15:30 mark ----
var bool  ibP_act  = false
var int   ibP_dir  = 0
var float ibP_rngP = na
var float ibP_p25  = na
var float ibP_p50  = na
var bool  ibP_r25  = false
var bool  ibP_r50  = false
var ibP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var ibP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var ibP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    ibP_act := false
if ib_broke and not ib_broke[1] and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_rng) and ib_rL > 0
    ibP_act  := true
    ibP_dir  := ib_dir
    ibP_rngP := ib_rng / ib_rL * 100
    ibP_p25  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * ib_rng
    ibP_p50  := ib_rL + 0.50 * ib_rng
    ibP_r25  := false
    ibP_r50  := false
    array.set(ibP_lv, 0, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 1, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 2, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 3, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 4, ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 5, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(ibP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(ibP_h50, k, false)
if ibP_act
    up    = ibP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not ibP_r25 and (up ? low <= ibP_p25 : high >= ibP_p25)
        ibP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not ibP_r50 and (up ? low <= ibP_p50 : high >= ibP_p50)
        ibP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(ibP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if ibP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h25, k, true)
        if ibP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(1, ibP_rngP, ibP_r25, ibP_r50, ibP_h25, ibP_h50)
        ibP_act := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- 15:30 ET mark + daily loss limit
// WITH "Hold trades until TP or SL" ON (the default) 15:30 CLOSES NOTHING. All it does is pull any UNFILLED
// entry limit so no order rests overnight - the per-engine cancels above already do that, and the sweep here
// repeats it by id so nothing can be left behind. A filled trade runs on with its stop and target into the
// evening, Asia, London and the next morning until one of the two prints.
//
// WITH THE SWITCH OFF this is the original EOD flatten, and it closes the POSITION, not a list of ids. Closing
// by id cannot be trusted for a flatten: it misses any id not on the list, and Pine NETS positions, so an order
// from one setup can end up reducing another setup's entry and leaving a remainder that no id on the list owns.
// ORDER MATTERS: cancel FIRST. A resting entry limit could still fill after the close, and a live exit order
// holds the position quantity reserved, which can leave the market close with nothing to close.
if ordersOn and flatten
    if holdToTPSL
        strategy.cancel("ORL")
        strategy.cancel("ORL2")
        strategy.cancel("ORS")
        strategy.cancel("ORS2")
        strategy.cancel("IBL")
        strategy.cancel("IBL2")
        strategy.cancel("IBS")
        strategy.cancel("IBS2")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-L")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-S")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RL")
        strategy.cancel("HAL-RS")
    else
        strategy.cancel_all()
        strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")

// The daily max loss is the ONE rule that reaches across setups AND survives the hold: it is an account circuit
// breaker, not a clock, so it closes everything that is open - a trade carried in from a previous session
// included - and cancels every resting order.
if dayHalt
    if ordersOn
        strategy.cancel_all()                      // exits included - they reserve the position and block the close
        strategy.close_all(comment = "Daily max loss")
    halTrDir := 0
    or_closed := true
    ib_closed := true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (fire once when each range breaks)
// The only alert() calls in the file, and they are addressed to a PERSON: the direction, the level that broke,
// and the planned entry, stop and target, so the trade can be placed by hand.
// A TradingView alert set to "alert() function calls only" carries EVERY alert() call in a script to whatever
// destination that one alert was given, so these cannot be split between a human and a machine. Point the
// alert at a notification channel, not at a broker webhook: TradingView sends anything that is not valid JSON
// as text/plain, and an order endpoint answers that with 415 "unsupported media type".
if brkAlerts and runHAL and (halBrkUp or halBrkDn)
    halSLa = halBrkUp ? f_halLongStop(hal15C) : f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    halTPa = halBrkUp ? f_halLongTP(hal15C, halSLa, halRR) : f_halShortTP(hal15C, halSLa, halRR)
    alert("HALYARD 15m BREAK  " + (halBrkUp ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halBrkUp ? halRH : halRL)) +
         "  | entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(hal15C)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halSLa)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halTPa)) +
         (holdToTPSL ? "  | hold until stop or target - may run overnight" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if brkAlerts and runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_broke[1]
    orTPa = f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    alert("ORB BREAK  " + (or_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)) +
         "  | pullback entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_e1)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(orTPa)) +
         (holdToTPSL ? "  | hold until stop or target - may run overnight" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if brkAlerts and runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_broke[1]
    ibTPa = f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    alert("IB BREAK  " + (ib_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)) +
         "  | pullback entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_e1)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ibTPa)) +
         (holdToTPSL ? "  | hold until stop or target - may run overnight" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ================================================================ Risk/Reward + fib tool (ALL THREE SETUPS)
// ONE routine draws every setup's box, so Halyard, ORB and IB are read the same way: a GREEN box from the entry
// to the target, a RED box from the entry to the stop, a border in the setup's colour (orange ORB, teal IB,
// fuchsia Halyard) and one label with that unit's contracts, $ risk, $ reward, R multiple and the 1-contract
// numbers.
// ANCHORING: y is price and x is BAR INDEX, both fixed at creation. The box is one bar wide to begin with and
// its right edge is extended bar by bar while the setup is live, so it always covers real bars - it never
// projects into empty space past the last bar. With the hold on, a trade that runs into the next session simply
// keeps growing its box, so a multi-day trade is drawn as one multi-day box.
// HISTORY: every valid setup keeps its boxes and fib lines, so you can scroll back and read the risk/reward of
// any past setup at the price levels it actually had. Only the text labels are capped by default.
var array<box>   dBox = array.new<box>()
var array<line>  dLin = array.new<line>()

// An ORB/IB setup draws up to FOUR boxes (first entry + average-down unit, two each) and three fib lines, so
// the per-setup limits are multiplied out here. Halyard draws two boxes. There are no R/R labels to cap any
// more - the text lives on the box itself, so it can never stack up into an unreadable pile.
f_trimDraws() =>
    if keepBox > 0
        while array.size(dBox) > keepBox * 4
            box.delete(array.shift(dBox))
        while array.size(dLin) > keepBox * 3
            line.delete(array.shift(dLin))

// Markup for ONE entry unit.
// d      = 1 long, -1 short.
// q      = contracts on THIS entry (each entry has its own count and its own risk budget).
// pv     = $ per point per contract used for the money figures. ORB/IB pass the "$ per point" input; Halyard
//          passes the symbol's own point value, which is what its position sizer divides by - so every box
//          reports the money that setup actually risks.
// ent2/q2= the OTHER unit, passed only on the first entry so its text can also show the setup total; pass
//          na/0 on an average-down unit and on Halyard, which has no second unit.
// dashed = draw this unit's boxes with a dashed border and a lighter fill, so an add is told apart at a glance.
//
// THE NUMBERS ARE WRITTEN ON THE BOX, NOT IN A LABEL. A label big enough for four lines of text sits on top of
// the price action it is describing, which is what made the old ones unreadable. One short line goes inside
// the REWARD box instead, pinned by text_valign to whichever edge of it IS the entry - the bottom for a long,
// the top for a short - so it annotates the 0 line and nothing else. It also cannot pile up: the text belongs
// to the box, so it disappears with it.
f_drawRR(int d, float ent, float zstop, float ptp, float q, color sigCol, string tag, float ent2, float q2, bool dashed, float pv) =>
    riskUsd = math.abs(ent - zstop) * pv * q
    rewUsd  = math.abs(ptp - ent) * pv * q
    rrr     = riskUsd > 0 ? rewUsd / riskUsd : na
    gCol = color.new(color.green, dashed ? 89 : 82)
    rCol = color.new(color.red,   dashed ? 89 : 82)
    txt = ""
    if showRRText
        txt := tag + " " + str.tostring(q, "#.#") + "c @" + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ent)) +
             "  " + str.tostring(rrr, "#.##") + "R  risk $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#")
        if not na(ent2) and q2 > 0
            totR = riskUsd + math.abs(ent2 - zstop) * pv * q2
            totW = rewUsd  + math.abs(ptp - ent2)  * pv * q2
            txt := txt + "  |  +add " + str.tostring(q2, "#.#") + "c @" + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ent2)) +
                 " -> setup $" + str.tostring(totR, "#") + " risk / $" + str.tostring(totW, "#") + " reward"
    bw = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ptp : ent, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? ent : ptp, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = gCol,
         text = txt, text_color = color.new(color.white, 10), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = d == 1 ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
    br = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ent : zstop, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? zstop : ent, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = rCol)
    if dashed
        box.set_border_style(bw, line.style_dashed)
        box.set_border_style(br, line.style_dashed)
    array.push(dBox, bw)
    array.push(dBox, br)
    [bw, br]

f_drawFibs(float rL, float rg, color sigCol, array<line> dest) =>
    array.clear(dest)
    for i = 1 to 3
        y = rL + i * 0.25 * rg
        ln = line.new(bar_index, y, bar_index + 1, y, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(sigCol, 35), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(dest, ln)
        array.push(dLin, ln)

// stretch one live unit's drawings to the current bar; prices stay exactly where they were set
f_growUnit(box bw, box br) =>
    if not na(bw)
        box.set_right(bw, bar_index)
        box.set_right(br, bar_index)

f_growFibs(array<line> fib) =>
    if array.size(fib) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fib) - 1
            line.set_x2(array.get(fib, i), bar_index)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- ORB drawings
// Drawn when the ENTRY ORDER IS ACTUALLY PLACED (or_placed / ib_placed), so a break that any filter rejects -
// wrong weekday, range too small, past the cutoff, IB already formed, double-break day, daily loss halt, sizing
// under one contract, or a limit waiting behind an open Halyard/ORB trade - draws nothing at all.
var box   orbBw  = na
var box   orbBr  = na
var box   orbBw2 = na            // the average-down unit's own pair of boxes
var box   orbBr2 = na
var bool  orbGrow = false
var array<line> orbFib = array.new<line>()
if runORB and or_placed and not or_placed[1] and not na(or_e1) and not na(or_zstop)
    orTP = f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    orbBw  := na
    orbBr  := na
    orbBw2 := na
    orbBr2 := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(or_rL, or_rng, color.new(color.orange, 0), orbFib)
    if showRR
        orbAdd = or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
        [bw, br] = f_drawRR(or_dir, or_e1, or_zstop, orTP, orbSz1, color.new(color.orange, 0), "ORB entry 1", orbAdd ? or_e2 : na, orbAdd ? orbSz2 : 0, false, ptVal)
        orbBw := bw
        orbBr := br
        if orbAdd and showRR2
            [bwA, brA] = f_drawRR(or_dir, or_e2, or_zstop, orTP, orbSz2, color.new(color.orange, 0), "ORB avg-down", float(na), 0.0, true, ptVal)
            orbBw2 := bwA
            orbBr2 := brA
    orbGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if orbGrow
    f_growUnit(orbBw,  orbBr)
    f_growUnit(orbBw2, orbBr2)
    f_growFibs(orbFib)
    // A FILLED trade's box stops growing when the trade closes, and only then - with the hold on that can be
    // days later. An UNFILLED setup's box still stops when its entry window shuts.
    if or_closed or (not holdToTPSL and flatten) or (not (or_f1 or or_f2) and not orbWin)
        orbGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- IB drawings
var box   ibBw  = na
var box   ibBr  = na
var box   ibBw2 = na             // the average-down unit's own pair of boxes
var box   ibBr2 = na
var bool  ibGrow = false
var array<line> ibFib = array.new<line>()
if runIB and ib_placed and not ib_placed[1] and not na(ib_e1) and not na(ib_zstop)
    ibTP = f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    ibBw  := na
    ibBr  := na
    ibBw2 := na
    ibBr2 := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(ib_rL, ib_rng, color.new(color.teal, 0), ibFib)
    if showRR
        ibAdd = ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
        [bw2, br2] = f_drawRR(ib_dir, ib_e1, ib_zstop, ibTP, ibSz1, color.new(color.teal, 0), "IB entry 1", ibAdd ? ib_e2 : na, ibAdd ? ibSz2 : 0, false, ptVal)
        ibBw := bw2
        ibBr := br2
        if ibAdd and showRR2
            [bwB, brB] = f_drawRR(ib_dir, ib_e2, ib_zstop, ibTP, ibSz2, color.new(color.teal, 0), "IB avg-down", float(na), 0.0, true, ptVal)
            ibBw2 := bwB
            ibBr2 := brB
    ibGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if ibGrow
    f_growUnit(ibBw,  ibBr)
    f_growUnit(ibBw2, ibBr2)
    f_growFibs(ibFib)
    if ib_closed or (not holdToTPSL and flatten) or (not (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ibWin)
        ibGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- HALYARD drawings
// Same box, same label, same growth rule as the two above - only the border colour differs. Halyard is a single
// unit, so there is no dashed average-down pair and no setup-total line. The money figures use the symbol's own
// point value, which is exactly what the Halyard position sizer divides by.
var box   halBw   = na
var box   halBr   = na
var bool  halGrow = false
if runHAL and halEntered and showRR and showRRHal
    halBw := na
    halBr := na
    [bwH, brH] = f_drawRR(halEntDir, halEnt, halStp, halTgt, halQty, halSigCol, halEntDir == 1 ? "HALYARD long" : "HALYARD short", float(na), 0.0, false, syminfo.pointvalue)
    halBw := bwH
    halBr := brH
    halGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if halGrow
    f_growUnit(halBw, halBr)
    if halTrDir == 0
        halGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy rules panel (top-right)
var table info = na
if showInfo and barstate.islast
    info := table.new(position.top_right, 1, 19, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), border_width = 1)
    table.cell(info, 0, 0,  (ordersOn ? "" : "[INDICATOR - no orders]  ") + "HALYARD + BREAK-THEN-PULLBACK (ORB + IB)",
         text_color = ordersOn ? color.aqua : color.orange, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 1,  "HALYARD: 15m candles built from chart bars - any chart TF",  text_color = color.fuchsia, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 2,  "  range = the 00:00 EST / 01:00 EDT 15m candle",             text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 3,  "  first 15m CLOSE beyond it trades | stop = far edge | R:R " + str.tostring(halRR, "#.##"), text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 4,  holdToTPSL ? "  one break per day | no day flat - runs to TP or SL" : "  one break per day | flat 13:30 / 14:30 ET",
         text_color = holdToTPSL ? color.lime : color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 5,  "Ranges: ORB 09:30-09:45 | IB 09:30-10:30 (ET)",              text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 6,  "Direction: low-first = LONG, high-first = SHORT",            text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 7,  (orbDepth >= 100 and ibDepth >= 100) ? "  close-depth filter: OFF (both at 100%)" : "  + close no deeper than " + str.tostring(orbDepth, "#") + "% (ORB) / " + str.tostring(ibDepth, "#") + "% (IB) into the range",
         text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 8,  "Enter AFTER the range breaks; limit at fib pullback:",       text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 9,  "  shallow -> 25% line | deeper -> 50% line",                 text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 10, "Stop: always the range extreme (100%)",                      text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 11, "Target: ORB L +10% / S +30% ; IB +30% extension",            text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 12, "Avg-down: 2nd unit @ 50% - own size & risk",                 text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 13, holdToTPSL ? "SEAT: Halyard > ORB > IB - one trade at a time, held across days" : "SEAT: Halyard > ORB > IB - one trade at a time",
         text_color = color.aqua, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 14, "No ORB carry: an unfilled ORB dies when the IB forms at 10:30", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 15, holdToTPSL ? "EXIT = TP or SL ONLY. 15:30 ET just kills unfilled orders." : "Skip double-break days | ORB/IB flatten 15:30 ET",
         text_color = holdToTPSL ? color.lime : color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 16, holdToTPSL ? "  -> use an EXTENDED-HOURS chart or overnight exits cannot fill" : "Toggle Run HAL / ORB / IB + weekdays to isolate results",
         text_color = holdToTPSL ? color.orange : color.aqua, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    ladderTxt = rmProg ? " rung " + (progLevel >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(progLevel) + " @ $" + str.tostring(progEq, "#") +
         " -> ORB " + str.tostring(progOrb1, "#.#") + "/" + str.tostring(progOrb2, "#.#") +
         ", IB " + str.tostring(progIb1, "#.#") + "/" + str.tostring(progIb2, "#.#") : sizeByRisk ? " (per entry, fixed capital)" : ""
    table.cell(info, 0, 17, modeTxt + ladderTxt + (maxDayLoss > 0 ? "  | day stop $" + str.tostring(maxDayLoss, "#") + (dayHalt ? " - HIT" : "") : ""), text_color = dayHalt ? color.red : color.yellow, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 18, brkAlerts ? "Break alerts: ON - manual notifications, no broker automation" : "Break alerts: off",
         text_color = brkAlerts ? color.lime : color.gray, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Probability table (ORB / IB setups only)
// Columns: N = sample size, Reach = how often that starting point is even reached, then the odds of price
// trading to each level from that starting point, before the 15:30 mark.
//   "From FILL" rows   : start = the entry fill, split by range size. Reach is n/a (the trade filled by definition).
//   "From 25% PB" rows : start = the moment price retraces to the 25% fib. Reach = share of armed setups that
//                        pull back that far. This is the number to read when your limit at the 25% line fills.
//   "From 50% PB" rows : same from the 50% fib - a deeper pullback, different odds, a smaller sample.
// Halyard is not in this table: it has no pullback entry and no range-extension targets, so none of these rows
// would mean anything for it.
tPos  = tblPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right : tblPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : tblPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_right
tRows = 8 + (pbSplit ? 12 : 4)

var table probTbl = na

f_tblRow(int row, string lbl, int nn, string reach, int t0, int t1, int t2, int t3, int q75, int q100, color txt, color bg) =>
    table.cell(probTbl, 0, row, lbl,                text_color = txt,          bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(probTbl, 1, row, str.tostring(nn),   text_color = color.white,  bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 2, row, reach,              text_color = color.silver, bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 3, row, f_pctStr(t0,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 4, row, f_pctStr(t1,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 5, row, f_pctStr(t2,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 6, row, f_pctStr(t3,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 7, row, f_pctStr(q75, nn),  text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 8, row, f_pctStr(q100, nn), text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)

// where we are right now, used to tint the row that applies (nothing is drawn on the chart)
cNow = color.new(color.blue, 40)      // the row that is live on this bar
cWas = color.new(color.blue, 78)      // a depth price has already passed through
cOff = color.black

if showTable and barstate.islast
    if na(probTbl)
        probTbl := table.new(tPos, 9, tRows, bgcolor = color.black, border_color = color.new(color.white, 70), border_width = 1, frame_color = color.white, frame_width = 1)
    // live state per strategy: 0 = not in play, 1 = broke, 2 = at the 25% pullback, 3 = at the 50% pullback
    stA  = array.from(orP_act ? (orP_r50 ? 3 : orP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0, ibP_act ? (ibP_r50 ? 3 : ibP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0)
    rgA  = array.from(orP_act ? orP_rngP : na, ibP_act ? ibP_rngP : na)
    filA = array.from(((or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed) ? 1 : 0, ((ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed) ? 1 : 0)
    hdr  = array.from("From FILL - by range size", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "STOP")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 0, array.get(hdr, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.white, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    // ---- section 1: from the fill, segmented by range size ----
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr = f_ranges(s)
        b1 = autoMode ? f_b1(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        b2 = autoMode ? f_b2(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        s1 = na(b1) ? "?" : str.tostring(b1, "#.##") + "%"
        s2 = na(b2) ? "?" : str.tostring(b2, "#.##") + "%"
        for bkt = 0 to 2
            [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5] = f_seg(s, bkt, b1, b2)
            here = hiLive and array.get(stA, s) > 0 and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), b1, b2) == bkt
            inTr = here and array.get(filA, s) == 1
            lbl  = (inTr ? "> " : "") + (bkt == 0 ? nm + " S <" + s1 : bkt == 1 ? nm + " M " + s1 + "-" + s2 : nm + " L >=" + s2)
            f_tblRow(s * 3 + bkt + 1, lbl, nn, "-", a2, a3, a4, a5, a1, a0, color.white, inTr ? cNow : here ? cWas : cOff)
    // ---- section 2: from the 25% / 50% pullback ----
    hdr2 = array.from("From PULLBACK", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "STOP")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 7, array.get(hdr2, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.new(color.aqua, 20), text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr2 = f_ranges(s)
        c1  = autoMode ? f_b1(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        c2  = autoMode ? f_b2(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm2 = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        st  = array.get(stA, s)
        for d = 0 to 1
            // the deepest pullback price has reached is "now"; a shallower one it already passed is tinted faintly
            depthOn = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st >= 2 : st >= 3)
            isNow   = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st == 2 : st == 3)
            if pbSplit
                for bkt = 0 to 2
                    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, bkt, c1, c2)
                    same = depthOn and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), c1, c2) == bkt
                    szn  = bkt == 0 ? "S" : bkt == 1 ? "M" : "L"
                    lbl  = ((same and isNow) ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " " + szn + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " PB"
                    f_tblRow(8 + s * 6 + bkt * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, (same and isNow) ? cNow : same ? cWas : cOff)
            else
                [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, -1, c1, c2)
                lbl = (isNow ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " pullback"
                f_tblRow(8 + s * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, isNow ? cNow : depthOn ? cWas : cOff)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Visuals
// ORB / IB levels
plot(runORB and not na(or_rH) ? or_rH : na, "ORB High", color = color.new(color.orange, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and not na(or_rL) ? or_rL : na, "ORB Low",  color = color.new(color.orange, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_e1) ? or_e1 : na, "ORB Entry", color = color.new(color.yellow, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_zstop) ? or_zstop : na, "ORB Stop", color = color.new(color.red, 25), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rH) ? ib_rH : na, "IB High", color = color.new(color.teal, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rL) ? ib_rL : na, "IB Low",  color = color.new(color.teal, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_e1) ? ib_e1 : na, "IB Entry", color = color.new(color.aqua, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_zstop) ? ib_zstop : na, "IB Stop", color = color.new(color.red, 25), style = plot.style_linebr)
// Halyard's 15-minute range, drawn from the engine's own candles
plot(runHAL and not na(halRH) ? halRH : na, "Halyard range high", color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runHAL and not na(halRL) ? halRL : na, "Halyard range low",  color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
// The breakout TRIANGLE marks the chart bar that closes the 15m candle which BREAKS the range.
plotshape(halShowMarker and halBrkUp, title = "Halyard: 15m close above range", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.abovebar, color = halUpCol, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(halShowMarker and halBrkDn, title = "Halyard: 15m close below range", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.belowbar, color = halDnCol, size = size.tiny)

// HALYARD DAY HIGHLIGHT. ORANGE = the Halyard day is Off. A faint GREEN / RED wash = the day is one-way, so the
// setting is readable off the chart instead of only out of the input dialog. Nothing is tinted on a two-way day.
halIsWeekday = halDow >= dayofweek.monday and halDow <= dayofweek.friday
bgcolor(not runHAL or not halIsWeekday ? na : not halDayOK ? color.new(color.orange, 95) : halMode == "Long" ? color.new(color.green, 96) : halMode == "Short" ? color.new(color.red, 96) : na, title = "Halyard day filter")
